<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:fa439ec4a2d8d0bd9abc5ecb0978a4481dc8cf7d> <http://schema.org/description> "This series provides an assessment of the 2011 epifaunal survey undertaken within and adjacent to the Tranche A development area of the planned Dogger Bank offshore wind farm (Creyke Beck) and along the proposed export cable route which extends from the south east corner of Dogger Bank to the East Yorkshire coast just south of Flamborough Head in the vicinity of Fraisthorpe. The survey was undertaken by Precision Marine Survey Ltd using the survey vessel ‘Mirage II’ in October and November 2011 and aimed to establish the abundance and composition of epifaunal communities (including demersal fish) within the survey area." .
_:e83cc69907f3dea8f61da07b19ddeeee <http://schema.org/value> "contaminant" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:fa3c6d8f29ceb51c77a2590f8ea6346f193166c8> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d21f79ee6b9c396cf61e3f3f8ca27374 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:fa3c6d8f29ceb51c77a2590f8ea6346f193166c8> <http://schema.org/description> "Surveys were undertaken in 2005 and 2006 with the objective of obtaining data on long term trends in contaminant persistence and biological recovery around a number of established producing fields selected on the basis of good long term monitoring data sets. Surveys were undertaken at Alba (in 2005), Beryl, Brae, Murchison and Nelson (all in 2006). The sampling and sample processing methods used were compatible with those used in previous operator surveys." .
_:d21f79ee6b9c396cf61e3f3f8ca27374 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
