_:d3848aac168a38769b596ef0a09888c6 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f67120e527951aa8922774196657b0d924cc6d2b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f67120e527951aa8922774196657b0d924cc6d2b> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned to assist in the archaeological assessment of the Humber Gateway OWF. The project comprised an assessment of 21 borehole logs and 60 Cone Penetrometry Testing (CPT) logs from 62 locations. The sediment sequences identified within the site are of low archaeological interest; however, reworked material of prehistoric archaeological interest may be preserved within the later geoarchaeological units." .
