_:d5c49d8e881eddded537b5d7b04ea2c1 <http://schema.org/value> "EIA" .
_:bd281ee706bcdbc81699431ec04eaa97 <http://schema.org/value> "basking shark" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f6421a7b5e686f7cee3815260dfc1bf74d0be23e> <http://schema.org/description> "This report presents the findings of the first year of bird surveys undertaken at Kyle Rhea to inform the EIA of the proposed Kyle Rhea Tidal Array.\r\nAlthough marine mammal and basking shark were surveyed as part of the same programme of fieldwork, the results of for these species are reported separately (Year 1 Marine Mammal and Basking Shark Report). The survey work is on-going and it is planned to complete to two full years of baseline characterisation studies." .
_:bd281ee706bcdbc81699431ec04eaa97 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cb7b528f3b0aa563a86709d46ce69295 <http://schema.org/value> "basking shark" .
_:c10736076fd8ab6e2323b8b5a8d9995d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ed87fd1c9357e04b5cfd42d5dbfa346a <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f639e2684d6b983351a43964b566dadc188da2aa> <http://schema.org/description> "In accordance with the FEPA licence, there is a requirement to undertake pre-construction and post-construction bathymetric surveys of a selection of turbine locations and the associated cable corridor to determine rates of scour around the turbines after construction. Emu Limited was commissioned by NEG Micon UK Ltd. to perform a series of hydrographic surveys of these areas in order to determine whether any souring occurs around the turbines or significant changes to the seabed profile have been made during construction of the windfarm. This project relates to the second post-construction swath survey which was carried out on 20th November 2005 from the vessel Emu surveyor." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f639e2684d6b983351a43964b566dadc188da2aa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ed87fd1c9357e04b5cfd42d5dbfa346a <http://schema.org/value> "NEG Micon UK Ltd." .
_:ed87fd1c9357e04b5cfd42d5dbfa346a <http://schema.org/value> "Emu Limited" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f639e2684d6b983351a43964b566dadc188da2aa> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ed87fd1c9357e04b5cfd42d5dbfa346a .
_:ed87fd1c9357e04b5cfd42d5dbfa346a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f634fda84c48ebaae9acf5a7624dd09a3e66aa58> <http://schema.org/description> "Sussex IFCA has historically undertaken fish surveys throughout the district in order to monitor juveniles of commercially important species and to further understanding of the ecosystem health, particularly within Marine Protected Areas. Seine net surveys have been undertaken since 2010 over Chichester Harbour, Cuckmere, Medmerry, Pagham Harbour, Rye Bay, and Tide Mills. Between 2011 and 2018, the Authority also undertook beam trawl surveys across Chichester Harbour and Rye Bay. Where possible, fish are identified to species level, although in some cases species are recorded at genus level. In each sample, 50 individuals of each species are are measured in total length, with any additional being counted. Once recorded, fish are returned alive to the sea." .
_:efae69a9eeb66c5660ae565afdc8d493 <http://schema.org/name> "taxon" .
