<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f55a2b61e90f2e7ee49c9618f8341aba467dc918> <http://schema.org/description> "This British Geological Survey (BGS) marine sampling survey took place in 1971 in the North Sea on board the MV Surveyor. The purpose was to investigate the geochemistry of the superficial sediments. Seabed samples were collected using a shipek grab. These data are archived by BGS. Technical details of the survey are contained in BGS Internal Report ?????. See geochemistry report WI/AC/85/1." .
