<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f434cf35bce1fe38e9004c9457a30dc6dbe05de3> <http://schema.org/description> "A pre-disturbance measured and photographic survey was carried out by a team led by the National Museum of Wales in 1992, following the find of a Hiberno-Norse sword guard by a member of the team in 1991. A site survey was produced, and the resulting report is cited as bibliography item no. 2. Prior to, alongside, and following the work; monitoring inspections of the site by the Archaeological Diving Unit (ADU) were carried out between 1991 and 1997. Both sets of work are recorded here. The coordinates given for the site are taken from the RCAHMW record for the site, the depths recorded are derived from ADU dive reports, and as the precise study area is not known, it has been recorded as 0 square metres." .
