<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f2dd55ed13d739be958782244e05ec71b7c86a16> <http://schema.org/description> "This sampling survey has been carried out by British Geological Survey (BGS) for BGS, the survey took place from June to July 1971 off the North of Scotland and in the Minch on board the MV Surveyor. The purpose was to collect data as part of UK regional mapping programme. Sample data were collected using dredge; drill; gravity corer; vibrocorer; Shipek grab and photography. These data are archived by BGS. No BGS survey report currently available, IGS 1971 annual report contains summary." .
