<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:f1d8651d87489f38bc3fad268aeb9c709a43eecf> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 82 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the North Atlantic Ocean area specifically the Ellett line CTD stations from Sound of Mull to Rockall, on the Wyville Thomson Ridge and in the Minch. The data were collected during July and August of 2003. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Association for Marine Science as part of the Northern Seas Programme (NSP)." .
