_:b5dda4631ffef912935f50bab76f1b8e <http://schema.org/value> "Thames" .
_:b5dda4631ffef912935f50bab76f1b8e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ebe90e81d21b4561d9f1a38612ada745f0f4c8fe> <http://schema.org/description> "The Gunfleet Sands site falls within the general area with a known history of human conflict. During the past two world wars the Thames and surrounds was mined and bombed by all parties and the legacy of these conflicts is the continued presence of unexploded ordnance (UXO). The potential for such material to be present during the development of the site must be considered and appropriate mitigation undertaken to reduce any risk. \r\nThis report evaluates the manipulation of existing data to establish its potential use in the detection of the likely presence of unexploded ordnance." .
_:b5dda4631ffef912935f50bab76f1b8e <http://schema.org/value> "Gunfleet Sands" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ebe90e81d21b4561d9f1a38612ada745f0f4c8fe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ebe90e81d21b4561d9f1a38612ada745f0f4c8fe> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b5dda4631ffef912935f50bab76f1b8e .
_:b5dda4631ffef912935f50bab76f1b8e <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ebe72e867c896d9b364c2575b6c433ab173b3978> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ba278b8163fe57249e2b26196b9b063b .
_:ba278b8163fe57249e2b26196b9b063b <http://schema.org/value> "UK Hydrographic Office" .
_:ba278b8163fe57249e2b26196b9b063b <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:ba278b8163fe57249e2b26196b9b063b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ba278b8163fe57249e2b26196b9b063b <http://schema.org/value> "National Monuments\r\nRecord" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ebe72e867c896d9b364c2575b6c433ab173b3978> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by AMEC Wind Energy and Renewable Energy\r\nSystems Ltd., on behalf of Centrica Renewable Energy Limited to undertake an\r\narchaeological desk-based assessment of the potential impact upon archaeological remains\r\nfrom the proposed cable route for the Docking Shoal Offshore Wind Farm (Wessex\r\nArchaeology 2006b), Race Bank Offshore Wind Farm (Wessex Archaeology 2006b) and\r\nLincs Offshore Wind Farm (Wessex Archaeology 2006a). This series relates to a proposed,\r\nalthough as yet unconfirmed cable route through the Wash.\r\nTo include all potential routes a broad Cable Route Study Area was created, covering the\r\neastern half of the Wash in a rough rectangle of approximately 48 by 20 kilometres.\r\nSearches for known archaeological material were conducted within the Study Area.\r\nInformation was sought from a wide range of local and national bodies, including the Historic\r\nEnvironment Record maintained by Norfolk County Council, the National Monuments\r\nRecord and the UK Hydrographic Office. The data were then filtered in order to focus only on\r\nthose sites that lie within the footprint of this scheme (i.e. up to the mean high water mark).\r\nThe remaining data were used as part of a wider assessment of archaeological potential. This series contains the assessment report and associated GIS data." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ebe72e867c896d9b364c2575b6c433ab173b3978> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ba278b8163fe57249e2b26196b9b063b <http://schema.org/value> "Norfolk County Council" .
_:ba278b8163fe57249e2b26196b9b063b <http://schema.org/value> "Centrica Renewable Energy Limited" .
