_:b1cb0006d86ed1cc5500496367d51006 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b1cb0006d86ed1cc5500496367d51006 <http://schema.org/value> "Centrica\r\nRenewable Energy Limited" .
_:b1cb0006d86ed1cc5500496367d51006 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:b72ee998dc4ced50bd7f351427766598 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ea362e5aee4878ca5f918c25ada403d5b3846c25> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by AMEC Power and Process Europe, on behalf of Centrica\r\nRenewable Energy Limited to undertake an archaeological interpretation of marine geophysical data for\r\nthe three proposed additional areas of Race Bank and Docking Shoal Offshore Wind Farms,\r\nassociated with the export cable routes. This report comprises the interpretation of multibeam\r\nbathymetry, magnetometer and sidescan sonar data and an archaeological impact assessment\r\ncovering the additional areas, and is in addition to and informed by the archaeological and impact\r\nassessments of the wind farms and cable routes conducted previously." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ea362e5aee4878ca5f918c25ada403d5b3846c25> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b72ee998dc4ced50bd7f351427766598 .
_:b6af5dc19461ab67e45bb8703e14a765 <http://schema.org/value> "St Bees Head" .
_:b6af5dc19461ab67e45bb8703e14a765 <http://schema.org/value> "Barrow-in-Furness" .
_:f71ca88cb4e98eed2ad42e5f81c9d1f4 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Nature Conservation Review" .
_:f71ca88cb4e98eed2ad42e5f81c9d1f4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ea324fef0bfc329a70631616c032facb1e6e5843> <http://schema.org/description> "This report was produced as part of the Marine Nature Conservation Review (MNCR) and presents data from 37 site surveys along the South Cumbrian coast (Barrow-in-Furness to St Bees Head). The sites visited included both rocky and sediment shores. The report includes site descriptions and locations, community/site type descriptions with abundances of characteristic species and a complete list of taxa recorded during the survey." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ea324fef0bfc329a70631616c032facb1e6e5843> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
