_:accb67aa3a7d7f9512f64379195aae8f <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e8908527db6a2c5a035774e00549591bb6e54c90> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e8908527db6a2c5a035774e00549591bb6e54c90> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:eeed0a828a146945afd8ab096aebc380 .
_:eeed0a828a146945afd8ab096aebc380 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:accb67aa3a7d7f9512f64379195aae8f <http://schema.org/value> "GS3 offshore Wind Farm" .
_:eeed0a828a146945afd8ab096aebc380 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:eeed0a828a146945afd8ab096aebc380 <http://schema.org/value> "DONG Energy" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e8908527db6a2c5a035774e00549591bb6e54c90> <http://schema.org/description> "In August 2010, DONG Energy was awarded a demonstration lease by The Crown Estate for a site to the south west of the GFS 2 array to construct two demonstration turbines with a maximum installed capacity of 20 MW together with associated inter-connecting cabling. This is known as the Gunfleet Sands 3 Demonstration Project (GFS 3).\r\n Applicable regulations will be followed for decommissioning of the onshore cable from landfall to the metering substation. Under Sections 105 to 114 of the Energy Act 2004 the Gunfleet Sands 3 â?? Demonstration Project is required to prepare and submit the decommissioning programme for the project prior to construction commencement. This document represents the preliminary decommissioning programme for the GS3 offshore Wind Farm and was submitted for approval in accordance with the Energy Act 2004 requirements. GS3 will also be decommissioned according to any lease conditions set out in the Crown Estate lease for this project.\r\n The decommissioning programme is informed and supported by the Environmental Statement (ES) for the GS3 Offshore Wind Farm Project that was submitted to the MMO Originally in December 2010, then an addendum was resubmitted to include the export cable in October 2011." .
_:eeed0a828a146945afd8ab096aebc380 <http://schema.org/value> "Crown Estate" .
_:accb67aa3a7d7f9512f64379195aae8f <http://schema.org/value> "Gunfleet Sands 3 Demonstration Project" .
_:fef6c995bb7d4509beefc8e22fc41488 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:e915c80428e4005c4cfe6a85c8756a13 <http://schema.org/value> "Department of Energy" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e8884845422300e76793069accbe486b1e1cec5f> <http://schema.org/description> "This high resolution marine multi-channel seismic survey commissioned by the Institute of Geological Sciences on behalf of Department of Energy took place in the Northern North Sea during 1st-27th November 1979 (Phase 1) aboard MV Aqua Star and 1st-14th February 1980 (Phase2) aboard Gardline Tracker. Phase 1 (Lines 1-5) was carried out by Fairfield Auatronics Ltd and Phase 2 (lines 5B-9) by Gardline surveys Ltd. Line coverage total 445km (Phase1 - 180km; Phase 2 - 265km). Sea floor data were collected using Echo sounder. Subsurface seismic data were gathered using a 9/15KJ sparker and line 4, Fairflex sleeve exploder. Survey details are contained in Fairfield and gardline acquisition reports and BGS technical report WB/MG/81/124." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e8884845422300e76793069accbe486b1e1cec5f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e915c80428e4005c4cfe6a85c8756a13 .
