<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e774c8da031dca6d3ec2173649819b2fd8ed7476> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f53ec4ca621ecb50455bf0db34b30483 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e774c8da031dca6d3ec2173649819b2fd8ed7476> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f148631cdb85054b009b8e519fb8f771 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e774c8da031dca6d3ec2173649819b2fd8ed7476> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 3 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the North Sea area specifically the Wee Bankie, Marr Bank, and Stonehaven, during September of 2002. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Fisheries Research Services Aberdeen Marine Laboratory." .
_:f148631cdb85054b009b8e519fb8f771 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:f53ec4ca621ecb50455bf0db34b30483 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f53ec4ca621ecb50455bf0db34b30483 <http://schema.org/value> "Wee Bankie" .
_:f53ec4ca621ecb50455bf0db34b30483 <http://schema.org/value> "Marr Bank" .
_:f148631cdb85054b009b8e519fb8f771 <http://schema.org/value> "Fisheries Research Services Aberdeen Marine Laboratory" .
_:f148631cdb85054b009b8e519fb8f771 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c11153059a3351ca261f6c2f82685eeb <http://schema.org/value> "Anglesey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e76f94968e42617b4f5e6d51cbb4f248f0e4c141> <http://schema.org/description> "This report delivers a Navigational Assessment and a Navigation Risk Assessment carried out by Marine &amp; Risk Consultants Limited (MARICO Marine) for Sea Generation (Wales) Ltd (SeaGen Wales) covering the\r\nconstruction, operation and decommissioning of the proposed Skerries Tidal Stream Array project, located between the coast of Anglesey and the offshore Skerries rocks; an area well known for strong tidal currents." .
_:c11153059a3351ca261f6c2f82685eeb <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:c11153059a3351ca261f6c2f82685eeb <http://schema.org/value> "Skerries rocks" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e76f94968e42617b4f5e6d51cbb4f248f0e4c141> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c11153059a3351ca261f6c2f82685eeb .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e76f94968e42617b4f5e6d51cbb4f248f0e4c141> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:c11153059a3351ca261f6c2f82685eeb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e76f61cfa8b765c362d14b40c0378fcdebca73c7> <http://schema.org/description> "This monograph summarises the great contribution of the MALSF to the study\r\nof submerged prehistory in the offshore areas of Britain. The review outlines the\r\ndevelopment of world-leading methodologies and successful integration of industrial\r\nand archaeological working practices. Focusing upon MALSF-financed research, a\r\nchronological synthesis of the archaeology and palaeo-landscape reconstructions\r\nfrom large regions of the southern North Sea, English Channel and elements of the\r\nwest coast encompasses much of the last 1 million years. The wide dissemination\r\nand contribution of this research to the understanding of the submerged prehistory\r\nof Northwest Europe and Britain is showcased. This substantial body of research\r\nserves as an exemplar of best-practice. The MALSF has enabled cross-disciplinary\r\ncollaboration to better manage, preserve and investigate the finite and internationallyimportant\r\narchaeology preserved offshore." .
