_:ab8676890259b729d48d56f49c3f2631 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ab8676890259b729d48d56f49c3f2631 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e735a9f776eb33cebf7f28057c2b23811f3caa24> <http://schema.org/description> "Report following a study of Morecambe Bays mudflats and sandflats. The study aimed to assess the condition of these intertidal areas with the aim of providing Natural England (NE) with a baseline on which to base future monitoring and surveillance.\r\n The report includes the distribution of biotopes within the Morecambe Bay Special Area of Conservation (SAC), species compositions and sediment characteristics. Further, the biotope information is comparred with that from previous studies and composition and distribution changes noted." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e7268e1916759e19c0eb49a87f2c7c83f77525dd> <http://schema.org/description> "The Port of London Authority (PLA) Hydrographic Service was commissioned by DONG\r\nEnergy to undertake a Multibeam Echosounder (MBES) survey at the Gunfleet Sands 3\r\nOffshore Windfarm in the Thames Estuary.\r\n\r\nThe scope of work, for the June 2015 survey included:\r\n1. MBES survey of 50m wide corridor along Export Cable Route between the\r\nWTG F0 and the HDD exit point [See Figure 1].\r\n2. MBES survey of the WTG foundations F00 and G00 and inter-array cable.\r\n\r\nThis series covers survey elements which were undertaken on the 20th &amp; 21st June 2015,\r\nalong the Export Cable Route and around Turbines F00 and G00. The survey work was\r\ncarried out using the PLA survey vessel ‘Yantlet’, with bathymetric data being collected using\r\na hull-mounted Reson SeaBat 8125h MBES." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e7268e1916759e19c0eb49a87f2c7c83f77525dd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
