<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e6fd6941108451ca35a38f4b6d98e00ea70150f9> <http://schema.org/description> "Samples and associated geological data are held at the British Geological Survey for Maritime Coastguard Agency (MCA), Civil Hydrography Programme (CHP), Bathymetric Survey HI1483; Thames Estuary Routine Resurvey 2015, TE5A Long Sand Head Full Area, Area in SqKm: 33; TE3A Sunk Focused Area, Area in SqKm: 9, (15/08/2015 to 03/10/2015), Standard: IHO S44ed5 Order 1a. Contract: RRS. FY 2015/16. Contractor: EGS." .
_:c582b63ae7c17076dfb6fec35632b96f <http://schema.org/value> "River Clyde" .
_:bf7cfa02d31dda4a01edde4de2057c6d <http://schema.org/value> "BGS" .
_:d5f5a9e2d429737c629cda2215d5d2ce <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d5f5a9e2d429737c629cda2215d5d2ce <http://schema.org/value> "sediment dredge" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:e6f2327a16ea814341ae06d9ffeb4a0627f25d75> <http://schema.org/description> "This British Geological Survey (BGS) marine sampling survey took place in 1969 in the River Clyde on board the RV Strathclyde. The purpose was to investigate the gravel distribution in the area. Seabed samples were collected using a shipek grab and sediment dredge, sediment cores were collected using a gravity corer. Beach samples were also collected. These data are archived by BGS. Technical details of the survey are contained in IGS Internal Report 73/9." .
