<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:dd1c85dcff469b872f8e2b14a5f3b1dd7f087b81> <http://schema.org/description> "The England's Historic Seascapes: Southwold to Clacton project was undertaken by Oxford Archaeology between April 2006 and 2007. The project is one of four pilot projects designed to apply the principles of HLC (Historic Landscape Characterisation) to the marine environment. This project built upon the intial methodology developed for the Liverpool Bay pilot study and seeks to develop MHLC (Marine Historic Landscape Characterisation) to ensure the final mehtodology is suitable to apply nationally. The project was funded by the Marine Aggregates Levy Sustainability Fund as rebursed by English Heritage." .
_:b3ca6088338d7ca6fd6564686179a0a0 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
