<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:d7b2ff168ef82dc797939464d655dbce297c2894> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises 20 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during 24 July to 15 August 2006 along two lines, one running approximately southwest from the Grand Banks, and a second running approximately southeast on the continental slope in front of Nova Scotia. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Proudman Oceanographic Laboratory as part of the Rapid Climate Change programme." .
