<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cf83e240ee8383019891274820f4d13217ac5915> <http://schema.org/description> "As an integral part of the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) for the proposed offshore wind\r\nfarm development on Gunfleet Sands, offshore Essex, Enron Wind Gunfleet Ltd commissioned an\r\noceanographic measurement programme. Thales Geosolutions (South Africa) (Pty) Ltd, hereafter\r\nreferred to as Thales, have been contracted to deploy two current/wave meters near Gunfleet Sands\r\nfor six months." .
_:b87f1680b1e5edf064db4a16f597dac6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c861d927b14a4ac212b73eeb28369359 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:c861d927b14a4ac212b73eeb28369359 <http://schema.org/value> "Gunfleet Sands" .
_:c861d927b14a4ac212b73eeb28369359 <http://schema.org/value> "Essex" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cf83e240ee8383019891274820f4d13217ac5915> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cf767c217142d5a37d2f23d7fef269ca1c0ee6b3> <http://schema.org/description> "This series is the Environmental Impact Assessment for the Thanet Offshore Wind Farm Project. Thanet Offshore Wind Limited (TOW), a subsidiary of Warwick Energy Limited (WEL), was created to develop opportunities for energy generation from renewable resources in the Thanet area. WEL successfully developed the Barrow Offshore Wind Farm project in Morecambe Bay, which is currently being constructed.\r\n\r\nTOW has been awarded the rights to develop an offshore wind farm in the Thames Estuary Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) area by The Crown Estate under Round Two of the offshore wind licensing arrangements. This is subject to TOW being successful in gaining the necessary consents for construction and operation of the wind farm." .
_:a73b742e574cfaedc0f7a370120aff61 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f26ad25473201182c05b81a10227067e <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
