_:e62521d09134e2df555f7103aa1e1786 <http://schema.org/value> "Natural England" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cdb3fed67b4938821a035e6b7f067fc086919d06> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:f1343286530f59acf67653a24ea8c75e <http://schema.org/value> "regulating order" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cdb3fed67b4938821a035e6b7f067fc086919d06> <http://schema.org/description> "The Solent currently exists as a public fishery but in the past has been managed through a regulating order (until 2010). In the 2013-2014 season, due a noted decline in the fishery, Southern IFCA used its â??Temporary Closure of Shellfish Beds Byelawâ?? to close the fishery in the wider Solent and only allowed fishing to continue for four weeks in Portsmouth and Langstone Harbours. The annual stock survey previously undertaken by CEFAS was discontinued in 2011. Due to the active management applied to the Solent oyster fishery by Southern IFCA, the authority decided that more recent data was required with regard to oyster levels in order to influence the management of the fishery. In a joint funded project with Natural England, Southern IFCA undertook an oyster survey following the same methodology as CEFAS in previous years, although station numbers in some areas were reduced. In addition to the CEFAS methodology, the survey design also considered the effectiveness of the Baird dredge by re-running a number of stations with the ladder dredge to work towards a comparison between the two dredges and, if further monitoring is required in years to come, move towards a method of fishing used by the industry." .
_:a808d5c0b6812560158334ff494d7e3d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:bb22a82e44a9f9a5e5746c8a4c53c1a6 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd988382aa36578474f5adb1df94bfb259cd360e> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bb22a82e44a9f9a5e5746c8a4c53c1a6 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd988382aa36578474f5adb1df94bfb259cd360e> <http://schema.org/description> "This processed bathymetric data set has been derived from an Unknown method survey. The source data was collected, validated and processed for the purpose of Safety Of Life At Sea (SOLAS). The data set must not be used for navigation or to create products that could be used for navigation." .
_:bb22a82e44a9f9a5e5746c8a4c53c1a6 <http://schema.org/value> "Unknown method survey" .
_:bb22a82e44a9f9a5e5746c8a4c53c1a6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd988382aa36578474f5adb1df94bfb259cd360e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 <http://schema.org/value> "vessel size" .
_:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 <http://schema.org/value> "vessel density" .
_:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 <http://schema.org/value> "engine power" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd80449e586212ced0d5e3617d4f45595a020eb1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd80449e586212ced0d5e3617d4f45595a020eb1> <http://schema.org/description> "This feature class contains interview data that has been summarised onto a grid of 3/4 of a nautical mile longitude and 3/8 of a nautical mile latitude. \r\n One condition of the research was that only those interviewees who explicitly gave permission for their data to be shared would have their own mapping represented in the final product shared with third parties. All other individuals have had their data removed from this feature class. Of 984 interviews, 594 gave their permission for their data to be shared.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has been included in this summary table only if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record.\r\n This data represents the activities of vessels under 15 metres in length. It does not distinguish between different gear glasses. \r\n The data is presented as a series of vessel counts per grid cell.\r\n In addition to presenting a record of vessel density, this feature class also describes demographic information on vessel size, engine power, crew size and construction date." .
_:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 <http://schema.org/value> "crew size" .
_:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 <http://schema.org/value> "construction date" .
_:d95ea367bdaac9cf962e8d83eb885680 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd80449e586212ced0d5e3617d4f45595a020eb1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ffef4b90e0381eeda745406c18507d00 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd719f005926c024536e358893ab3244f0938315> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd719f005926c024536e358893ab3244f0938315> <http://schema.org/description> "This data set consists of a bathymetric grid derived from multibeam bathymetry data from cruise JC071. The bathymetric grid was created by gridding the cleaned raw multibeam data from JC071 at 1/64 arc-minute intervals using a nearneighbour gridding algorithm from the Generic Mapping Tools (GMT) software system. The data set covers an approximate one degree square with the minimum and maximum longitude and latitude co-ordinates: 17.016667W-16.216667W; 48.78333N-49.28333N. This is located in the Northeast Atlantic Ocean area. The data were collected from 7th-8th May 2012 using an EM120 Multibeam Echo-sounder. The cruise was part of the Porcupine Abyssal Plain (PAP): sustained ocean observation project. The bathymetry data were collected on an opportunistic basis during the cruise. The cruise was operated by the National Oceanography Centre (NOC), equipment operated by National Marine Facilities Sea Systems. The bathymetric grid was created by BODC for contributing to the EMODnet High Resolution Seafloor Mapping (HRSM) Project." .
_:ffef4b90e0381eeda745406c18507d00 <http://schema.org/value> "BODC" .
_:ffef4b90e0381eeda745406c18507d00 <http://schema.org/value> "National Oceanography Centre" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cd719f005926c024536e358893ab3244f0938315> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ffef4b90e0381eeda745406c18507d00 .
_:ffef4b90e0381eeda745406c18507d00 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:ffef4b90e0381eeda745406c18507d00 <http://schema.org/value> "National Marine Facilities Sea Systems" .
_:bded58d4e4b7d99fccfe8998b81f9199 <http://schema.org/value> "Wyville-Thomson Ridge" .
