<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:cc1bafc3db544dacef1b389cecb34857791cb9b0> <http://schema.org/description> "This British Geological Survey (BGS) marine sampling survey took place in October 1971 in the Moray Firth on board the fishing vessel ?. The purpose was to obtain data for regional geology mapping. Sea-bed samples and photographs were collected by divers. These data are archived by BGS. Technical details of the survey are contained in report ?????." .
