_:dcec40494437bda00e847469f8870b94 <http://schema.org/value> "Firth of Clyde" .
_:dcec40494437bda00e847469f8870b94 <http://schema.org/value> "Great Cumbrae Island" .
_:dcec40494437bda00e847469f8870b94 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:bdfc83aa50ba481ac936ddd60449ae03b49c5472> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:dcec40494437bda00e847469f8870b94 <http://schema.org/value> "Kames Bay" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:bdfc83aa50ba481ac936ddd60449ae03b49c5472> <http://schema.org/description> "A continuous long term study into the physical features of a sandy shore (Kames Bay) was carried out by students during a marine biology field course at the University Marine Biological Station Millport (UMBSM). The sheltered beach at Kames Bay is a site of special scientific interest (SSSI) and is situated on the southern coast of Great Cumbrae Island, Firth of Clyde." .
_:dcec40494437bda00e847469f8870b94 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:bdfc83aa50ba481ac936ddd60449ae03b49c5472> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:dcec40494437bda00e847469f8870b94 .
