<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba8528ecac9b27f2a61e2e53479b492f8366d164> <http://schema.org/description> "Benthic monitoring of the sea bed adjacent to the fish farm as a requirement of the CAR licence for the site. Grab samples collected in proximity to the farm and at two reference locations. Samples analysed for: benthos, redox, psa, carbon." .
_:a29c10d9d02008691db6d49c7af37dc5 <http://schema.org/name> "policies" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba816701ae9ae03557d79f8bc8b1cd8175ee4aa0> <http://schema.org/description> "This document within this series presents the decommissioning programme for TOW and is being submitted for approval in accordance with the Energy Act 2004 requirements. TOW will be decommissioned according to the lease conditions set out in the Crown Estate lease for this project.\r\nThe decommissioning programme is informed and supported by the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) for the TOW Project that was submitted to the Offshore Renewables Consents Unit which was part of the Department of Trade and Industry and to Redcar and Cleveland Borough Council in 2004.\r\nThis plan is to be reviewed and revised periodically throughout the lifecycle of the project to reflect changing circumstances and regulatory requirements, and to incorporate improvements in understanding of the marine environment and technology." .
_:acf520299582f125e177e426ccffc728 <http://schema.org/value> "Redcar" .
