_:bc98dc430831563af4dc39d79e35ac96 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:bc98dc430831563af4dc39d79e35ac96 <http://schema.org/value> "Zone 9 Irish Sea" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba4e0c9392ad664bdcd50a29a6046b1a3498193c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bc98dc430831563af4dc39d79e35ac96 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba4e0c9392ad664bdcd50a29a6046b1a3498193c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a884894da3f2b456e41d73a5253769f9 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:ba4e0c9392ad664bdcd50a29a6046b1a3498193c> <http://schema.org/description> "Centrica Energy Renewable Investments Limited (CERI) now Celtic Array commissioned Wessex Archaeology to undertake this review. This review was undertaken between and April and October 2012 A total of 43 borehole sequences in the Zone 9 Irish Sea (SE Development) Area have been reviewed as part of a Stage 1 geoarchaeological desk-based assessment. The was undertaken as part of a programme of baseline data gathering currently undertaken by Centrica Energy Renewable Investments Limited (CERI) now Celtic Array for the Irish Sea Zone.. The results of the geoarchaeological review indicate Pleistocene and Holocene glacial and marine sediments present across the study area and confirm the earlier findings within this area undertaken as part of Met Mast Geotechnical Assessment (Wessex Archaeology 2011). This review makes recommendations for a total of 13 partial sequences to proceed to Stage 2 recording and sampling Corresponding Centrica Document No: SE-D-CE-073-0000-000000-011 Available dataset : Reports in pdf formats, GIS data in shapefile and geodatabase format, 3dmodels" .
_:a884894da3f2b456e41d73a5253769f9 <http://schema.org/value> "Celtic Array" .
