_:d213c862a1799345cc87ee5f9bb4983a <http://schema.org/value> "Single Beam Bathymetry" .
_:b8af5171a2b9a9214b573a47e2f37f0c <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b959354528a9c4184e7a32e2a1cf0b6209d26aae> <http://schema.org/description> "Project Number:\r\nCS0439. In June 2014, Titan Environmental Surveys were commissioned by Dong Energy to conduct a geophysical and bathymetric survey for an area of Export Cable Route not previously surveyed. The objectives of the survey were to collect Geophysical and Bathymetric data around the area where the cable had been laid outside of the original survey limits, checking for depth of burial or any cable exposure.\r\nThe survey would be undertaken with Single Beam Bathymetry, Swathe Bathymetry, Side Scan Sonar (SSS) Sub Bottom Profiler and Magnetometer." .
_:b8af5171a2b9a9214b573a47e2f37f0c <http://schema.org/value> "depth" .
_:a1ed278093caee8f88506d7983fa1fcb <http://schema.org/value> "Titan Environmental Surveys" .
_:a1ed278093caee8f88506d7983fa1fcb <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:d213c862a1799345cc87ee5f9bb4983a <http://schema.org/value> "Swathe Bathymetry" .
_:b0c808aaf12084196681b2e85a5121ef <http://schema.org/value> "Marine and Coastal Access Bill" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b950b1bd3bfddbcc73037a421495754157d0d56c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b0c808aaf12084196681b2e85a5121ef .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b950b1bd3bfddbcc73037a421495754157d0d56c> <http://schema.org/description> "This layer shows the area in which peat exposures are liekly to occur. This may indicate the potential for the presence of peat and clay exposure communities.\r\n Method: Data from Archeological sources including the English Heritage database was used to identify area where peat exposures were liekly to occur. \r\n This layer forms one of a set of data layers created for the Defra MB0102 contract. This work will support the delivery of a network of Marine Protected Areas as required to meet existing international and national obligations and commitments, including Marine Conservation Zones (MCZs), a new measure to be delivered as part of the Marine and Coastal Access Bill, and equivalent measures under Scottish legislation. The availability of these data layers will also be of importance in underpinning Marine Planning (e.g. licensing) in our marine area." .
_:b0c808aaf12084196681b2e85a5121ef <http://schema.org/name> "policies" .
_:b0c808aaf12084196681b2e85a5121ef <http://schema.org/value> "Scottish legislation" .
_:b0c808aaf12084196681b2e85a5121ef <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b950b1bd3bfddbcc73037a421495754157d0d56c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ae0681d6cc3b8c950ec49ed6c6a1d240 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b94340cfdbd34cf49f4f2355460abca93b8b8501> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ae0681d6cc3b8c950ec49ed6c6a1d240 .
_:ae0681d6cc3b8c950ec49ed6c6a1d240 <http://schema.org/value> "Fisheries Mapping Project" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b94340cfdbd34cf49f4f2355460abca93b8b8501> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bfb79cbdc28784d3cd2f80e9347515e .
_:ae0681d6cc3b8c950ec49ed6c6a1d240 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b94340cfdbd34cf49f4f2355460abca93b8b8501> <http://schema.org/description> "This layer is the output of the Eastern Sea Fisheries Joint Committee's Fisheries Mapping Project, which aimed to describe-using best available data and fishermens knowledge-the extent of the main fisheries within the ESFJC District.\r\n \r\n They are not, however, exhaustive-please use with discretion. Use of this data should never replace full, proper consultation within the fishing industry, but rather be seen as illustrative of the types of activity within the District and, where information is available, an indication of seasonality. \r\n \r\n A report on the Fisheries Mapping Project will be available in Spring 2012, and will contain information about how the data was collected and compiled, and the process of consultation which was undertaken. Please refer to the ESFJC website: www.eastern-ifca.gov.uk\r\n \r\n For further details on the project, its output, or guidance on how to interpret the data, please contact the project manager: jwoo@esfjc.co.uk.\r\n \r\n To register for updates to these layers (including forthcoming addition of metadata), please register your interest at jwoo@esfjc.co.uk. \r\n \r\n (Please acknowledge use of Fisheries Mapping Project data. It can be cited as: ESFJC, 2010- ESFJC District Fisheries Mapping Project)." .
_:bfb79cbdc28784d3cd2f80e9347515e <http://schema.org/value> "Eastern Sea Fisheries Joint Committee" .
_:bfb79cbdc28784d3cd2f80e9347515e <http://schema.org/value> "ESFJC" .
_:bfb79cbdc28784d3cd2f80e9347515e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b94340cfdbd34cf49f4f2355460abca93b8b8501> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:bfb79cbdc28784d3cd2f80e9347515e <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b93a6010bdafae82e7401c19e49a5ac1e95a1d1d> <http://schema.org/description> "The aim of this project is to develop written guidance for developers to assist in the process of\r\nthe assessment of cumulative impacts of wind farms on bird populations.\r\nThe project, managed by a steering group, determined that the guidance should be based on\r\nscientific principles, recommend methodologies robust enough to meet statutory requirements\r\nand be practicable for developers within the time frames and resources normally available for\r\nenvironmental impact assessment." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:b93a6010bdafae82e7401c19e49a5ac1e95a1d1d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
