<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a81e2344ef587793337873ac8cc53308722a37c8> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 8 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the Irish Sea and surrounding regions (Celtic Sea, St. George's Channel, North Channel and Clyde Sea) during November 1979. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the University of Wales, Bangor School of Ocean Sciences." .
_:a8c052de9c8a7320468a6450cfc6cd12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d1c53b4a333341d28159f78dc2bb5249 <http://schema.org/value> "public awareness projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a81a3b524db16023ef3b998fe03f45b730b6bc64> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d1c53b4a333341d28159f78dc2bb5249 .
_:a8c052de9c8a7320468a6450cfc6cd12 <http://schema.org/value> "South West England" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a81a3b524db16023ef3b998fe03f45b730b6bc64> <http://schema.org/description> "The objectives of this study were: To raise awareness of the marine environment through a programme of outreach work in schools across South West England, designed to fit in with the national curriculum; To raise wide awareness of the integrated role of science, industry and management in society\\'s use of marine resources; To disseminate information on the marine environment in a balanced manner relative to the sustainable use and conservation of natural resources; To build partnerships with other individuals, organisations and other outreach programmes to ensure the continuation of marine education and outreach in future years; and To collect feedback from the contacts and events, learning from the experience for future public awareness projects." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a81a3b524db16023ef3b998fe03f45b730b6bc64> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:a8c052de9c8a7320468a6450cfc6cd12 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:d1c53b4a333341d28159f78dc2bb5249 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a81a3b524db16023ef3b998fe03f45b730b6bc64> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a8c052de9c8a7320468a6450cfc6cd12 .
_:d1c53b4a333341d28159f78dc2bb5249 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a7fb277431fea18755200d5b0772b53088766fa7> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 76 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the North Sea and the North East Atlantic Ocean (limit 40W) area specifically the along the Fair Isle-Munken (Faroe), Nolso (Faroe)-Flugga (Shetland), standard JONSIS, East Shetland (ES) and northern North Sea (EC) standard sections. The data were collected during December of 1992. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Scottish Office Agriculture and Fisheries Department Aberdeen Marine Laboratory." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a7fb277431fea18755200d5b0772b53088766fa7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
