_:ab423025e862f86d9a71d0ebe0116ad7 <http://schema.org/value> "Princess Elizabeth Trough" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a7bba6b30f5181f40360510c392b329a61fff4cc> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 32 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during February - March 1994. The cruise, part of the World Ocean Circulation Experiment (WOCE) Indian Special Survey (ISS01), worked stations in the Southern Indian Ocean, specifically the Crozet Basin, a section from Crozet Is. - Kerguelen Is., Princess Elizabeth Trough and the Madagascar Basin. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Food Lowestoft Fisheries Laboratory as part of the World Ocean Circulation Experiment (WOCE)." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a7a84a77a8bb521491e80c8ef9077354bafadb1b> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fb1fd0951197ebbec53644b554954419 .
