<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5f7678b8daf74643841eb043a396357d469db46> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f67ee71b00c20c2948784ac2bff909cd .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5f7678b8daf74643841eb043a396357d469db46> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:de72c608378d5309e98c8f2b08733923 .
_:f67ee71b00c20c2948784ac2bff909cd <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5f7678b8daf74643841eb043a396357d469db46> <http://schema.org/description> "As part of an investigative program for the proposed disposal of dredged material at sea BODL engaged Partrac Ltd (Partrac) to undertake an assessment of sediment dispersion potential associated with the deposition of dredged material to be generated during gravity based foundation (GBF) installation operations at Array 2 at the Blyth offshore wind farm (BOW) site. Specifically, Partrac was requested to quantitatively evaluate the sediment dispersion potential within the surrounding North Sea associated with a proposed surface disposal of material from a trailing suction hopper dredger. The report is written to inform a variation application to the marine licence and consequently forms part of the application documents, specifically to assess likely impacts upon the local Marine Conservation Zone (MCZ, St Marys to Coquet Island) that was formally designated in January 2016.\r\nTo evaluate the sediment dispersion potential associated with the proposed disposal site, Partrac have employed a cumulative numerical modelling approach that can replicate sediment plume simulations. The regional modelling was undertaken using a two-dimensional (2D) approach, to properly capture the relevant physical processes. The 2014 version (Service Pack 1) of the MIKE21 from the MIKEZero software was used to set-up and operate a European scale two-dimensional (depth-averaged) flexible mesh model. The MIKE21-HD (Hydro-Dynamic) and MIKE21-PT (Particle-Tracking) modules were applied to investigate tidal and sediment plume dispersion processes at a regional and local scale, respectively. Site specific field measurements were utilised to support the numerical model development and verification." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5f7678b8daf74643841eb043a396357d469db46> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b0575e8edccec2b7474aa33fa97a13a0 .
_:f67ee71b00c20c2948784ac2bff909cd <http://schema.org/value> "North Sea" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5f7678b8daf74643841eb043a396357d469db46> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:f67ee71b00c20c2948784ac2bff909cd <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:ae444e8f24c72abbcc1c7feb7533a41a <http://schema.org/value> "Isle of Man" .
_:b3a541c9263a6ce500a6454e3dd4a2eb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5f65d55e66d27673713fb0fdbf6af1ec5aa99d3> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ae444e8f24c72abbcc1c7feb7533a41a .
_:b3a541c9263a6ce500a6454e3dd4a2eb <http://schema.org/value> "on Ministry of Defence" .
_:e0523f23d338fe6c254d6a964e660947 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:b3a541c9263a6ce500a6454e3dd4a2eb <http://schema.org/value> "Renewable Energy Systems Ltd" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5f65d55e66d27673713fb0fdbf6af1ec5aa99d3> <http://schema.org/description> "This assessment was prepared by Renewable Energy Systems Ltd (“RES”). and the report presents an assessment of the Round 3 Offshore Irish Sea Zone and the potential impact that the projects may have on nearby aviation facilities like the on Ministry of Defence , NERL and the Isle of Man airport infrastructure\r\n\r\nThe proposed Round 3 Offshore Irish Sea zone is situated off the west coast of England and south east of the Isle of Man. Due to the large extent of the area a zonal approach was undertaken to assess the potential environmental impacts. The majority of sites lie beneath controlled airspace corridors including the south eastern extent of the Isle of Man CTA1, L10, L70 &amp; L90. The nearest aerodrome is the Isle of Man airport which is approximately 27km (14.5nm) to the edge of the nearest site; there are additionally a number of heliports on the eastern side of the project mainly concentrated around the Morecambe gas field.\r\n\r\nAvailable dataset : GIS outputs- MXD and Shapefiles; Drawings and Reports in PDF\r\n\r\nCorresponding Centrica Document No: R3-D-EN-130-0000-000000-001" .
_:e0523f23d338fe6c254d6a964e660947 <http://schema.org/value> "zonal approach" .
_:b3a541c9263a6ce500a6454e3dd4a2eb <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:ae444e8f24c72abbcc1c7feb7533a41a <http://schema.org/value> "England" .
