<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5df8eedf402813c05e2f97e721fbf79d43785f2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:c539d4b1550a55c4ce6c59aa0bd81ea <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5df8eedf402813c05e2f97e721fbf79d43785f2> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c539d4b1550a55c4ce6c59aa0bd81ea .
_:c539d4b1550a55c4ce6c59aa0bd81ea <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:c539d4b1550a55c4ce6c59aa0bd81ea <http://schema.org/value> "LiDAR measurements" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5df8eedf402813c05e2f97e721fbf79d43785f2> <http://schema.org/description> "In addition to the Race Bank Meteorological Mast ENGrbcM50 logging system and instrumentation, a WindCube V2 LiDAR was\r\ninstalled on the Race Bank offshore platform in December 2010.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of this installation was twofold:\r\nAs the level of IEC non-compliance varies across instruments on the Race Bank mast, LiDAR measurements were used to facilitate tower shadow corrections and gauge the consequent reduction of mast measurement uncertainty; \r\nThe LiDAR measurements were also used for shear verification purposes." .
_:a8455e33beddec1a5875247db4be13d5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:a8455e33beddec1a5875247db4be13d5 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Environmental Data and Information Network" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5ddc3dd853efe40005e1534ee18ae1d15900124> <http://schema.org/description> "MBES (MultiBeamEchoSounder) bathymetry and backscatter data obtained using a Simrad EM710. These data are archived with the Marine Environmental Data and Information Network (MEDIN) Data Archive Centres (DACs) including the British Geological Survey (BGS) DAC for geology and geophysics, The Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data (DASSH) and the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) bathymetry DAC. The full site data package including raw is also available on request from BGS." .
_:a8455e33beddec1a5875247db4be13d5 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5ddc3dd853efe40005e1534ee18ae1d15900124> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5ddc3dd853efe40005e1534ee18ae1d15900124> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a8455e33beddec1a5875247db4be13d5 .
_:a8455e33beddec1a5875247db4be13d5 <http://schema.org/value> "Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data" .
_:a8455e33beddec1a5875247db4be13d5 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:a8455e33beddec1a5875247db4be13d5 <http://schema.org/value> "United Kingdom Hydrographic Office" .
_:ade609de6577df86534448cd0e22d379 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5c1389a5e1fba0b3aded8c89e48bad61f580864> <http://schema.org/description> "Samples and associated geological data are held at the British Geological Survey for Maritime Coastguard Agency (MCA), Civil Hydrography Programme (CHP), Bathymetric Survey HI1482; East Anglia Routine Resurvey 2015, EA10 Stanford Channel Focussed Area B, Area in SqKm: 1; EA10 Stanford Channel Focussed Area A, Area in SqKm: 1; EA12a Lowestoft South Road, Area in SqKm: 2; EA9 Holm Channel Focused Area, Area in SqKm: 12; EA3 Cockle Shoal Focussed Area B, Area in SqKm: 0; EA3 Cockle Shoal Focused Area A, Area in SqKm: 1, (21/09/2015 to 09/12/2015), Standard: IHO S44ed5 Order 1a. Contract: RRS. FY 2015/16. Contractor: EGS." .
_:ade609de6577df86534448cd0e22d379 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5c1389a5e1fba0b3aded8c89e48bad61f580864> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5c1389a5e1fba0b3aded8c89e48bad61f580864> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ade609de6577df86534448cd0e22d379 .
_:ade609de6577df86534448cd0e22d379 <http://schema.org/value> "Maritime Coastguard Agency (MCA)" .
_:ade609de6577df86534448cd0e22d379 <http://schema.org/value> "Civil Hydrography Programme" .
_:ade609de6577df86534448cd0e22d379 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:ade609de6577df86534448cd0e22d379 <http://schema.org/value> "EGS" .
_:b02d6368df2e17614f6cf891b7d38dd3 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5b927091a3dd14f1f840d4361386748a8b3bf24> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b02d6368df2e17614f6cf891b7d38dd3 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5b927091a3dd14f1f840d4361386748a8b3bf24> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:b02d6368df2e17614f6cf891b7d38dd3 <http://schema.org/value> "tidal currents" .
_:b02d6368df2e17614f6cf891b7d38dd3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c7ebe46249c4f71e49ce1decfb3f94bd <http://schema.org/value> "bathymetric\r\nsurvey" .
_:c7ebe46249c4f71e49ce1decfb3f94bd <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5b927091a3dd14f1f840d4361386748a8b3bf24> <http://schema.org/description> "In order to accurately assess the potential of a particular location to provide a dependable and\r\nsustainable marine energy resource, it is essential to have a thorough knowledge of the site in terms of\r\nseabed morphology and local tidal flow regime. Prior to the undertaking of this particular measurement\r\ncampaign, the former aspect was obtained by the Client from data provided by a recent bathymetric\r\nsurvey. This enabled the most suitable sites to be identified for the study of the tidal flow aspect.\r\nWallingford Environmental Surveys Ltd (WES Ltd) was therefore commissioned in July 2008 to\r\nmeasure the tidal currents at three specified fixed (static) locations for a period of 30 days. Vesselborne\r\n(dynamic) current measurements were also undertaken throughout the area of interest to augment\r\nthe data from the static devices to enable mapping of the spatial variation of the tidal flow by\r\nextrapolation." .
_:c7ebe46249c4f71e49ce1decfb3f94bd <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5b927091a3dd14f1f840d4361386748a8b3bf24> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c7ebe46249c4f71e49ce1decfb3f94bd .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5b56a07d6ad7a1d16bd6bfc399abd2e690367f8> <http://schema.org/description> "NWP Offshore Ltd have commissioned Arup for an assessment of\r\nthe socio-economic impact of the proposed North Hoyle Offshore\r\nWind Farm development." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5b56a07d6ad7a1d16bd6bfc399abd2e690367f8> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c24148992fc765e02e7319f933a77279 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5b56a07d6ad7a1d16bd6bfc399abd2e690367f8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:c24148992fc765e02e7319f933a77279 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c24148992fc765e02e7319f933a77279 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:c24148992fc765e02e7319f933a77279 <http://schema.org/value> "Arup" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5a981a2dffbb2449ecc5fc5d125a4d8352d784c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:add9420dfb5711ade70fccb674d7423f .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5a981a2dffbb2449ecc5fc5d125a4d8352d784c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bfe9a5743d54c05294209f17ef926342 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5a981a2dffbb2449ecc5fc5d125a4d8352d784c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:a5a981a2dffbb2449ecc5fc5d125a4d8352d784c> <http://schema.org/description> "During October and November 2006 Gardline Environmental Ltd performed an environmental survey in UKCS 49/19 and 49/24, around the Indefatigable Juliet ('Inde J') platforms, for Shell U.K. Ltd. The objective of this environmental survey was to provide an environmental baseline assessment for the decommissioning program and post-decommissioning monitoring." .
_:bfe9a5743d54c05294209f17ef926342 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:add9420dfb5711ade70fccb674d7423f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
