_:b058e88ec3c796aeb42d43513b78a50d <http://schema.org/value> "Celtic Array" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a84c184658c1b6bcf76d2e8d1b7ca5ba06d9f25> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b5038d9f985377caee56dea114566030 .
_:b5038d9f985377caee56dea114566030 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b058e88ec3c796aeb42d43513b78a50d <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:b058e88ec3c796aeb42d43513b78a50d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b5038d9f985377caee56dea114566030 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a84c184658c1b6bcf76d2e8d1b7ca5ba06d9f25> <http://schema.org/description> "ABP Marine Environmental Research Ltd (ABPmer) , commissioned by Celtic Array had provided previous metocean studies which reviewed the anticipated metocean conditions expected across the Irish Sea Zone, and also identified and collated a range of metocean data and asuch defined a 12 month survey programme in order to fill strategic data gaps and provide new information to fulfil the project’s (proposed Round 3 development) requirement. As a result of this, a data sufficiency exercise was established for the metocean information to support this requirement. This exercise considered in more detail the range of present metocean data available to help establish the anticipated synoptic behaviour in waves and tides over the 12 month survey programme and to set appropriate criteria for the metocean survey.\r\n\r\nAssociated report :R3-D-EN-128-0000-501006-016" .
_:e97672f2732f83571ed08463278c8ee6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a84c184658c1b6bcf76d2e8d1b7ca5ba06d9f25> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b058e88ec3c796aeb42d43513b78a50d .
_:a79b392d2d327f20021a9d2f381b35a9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:a79b392d2d327f20021a9d2f381b35a9 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a6be1f509c27f0d26f43fe6922e9e9e9f1d2eda> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class records the number of individuals involved in the anchoring of boats at angling sites on a monthly basis. The month fields record the number of interviewees that have contributed to this data, the fields with a count suffix record the number of individuals. Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record.\r\n Anchoring was poorly reported within the anchoring interviews, anchoring will be taking place at many off shore angling sites." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a6be1f509c27f0d26f43fe6922e9e9e9f1d2eda> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a6be1f509c27f0d26f43fe6922e9e9e9f1d2eda> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a79b392d2d327f20021a9d2f381b35a9 .
_:a79b392d2d327f20021a9d2f381b35a9 <http://schema.org/value> "Stakmap/Fishermap" .
_:e6784c628e8dc459dadd70756d576de1 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a4e5cdca7f5b0b7cab0a9151c06b52a64976acc> <http://schema.org/description> "Nearly 300 wood identifications were carried out on wooden artefacts recovered from the wreck of the London during phases of surface recovery and archaeological excavation between 2014 and 2016. A total of 16 wood (/wood group) types were identified, of which 14 were hardwoods and two were softwoods. Patterns of wood selection preferences for some of the artefact types have been recognised, in particular for the handspikes and pulley blocks. Wood choices likely reflect characteristics of the wood types themselves (for example, ease of working, comfort in use) as well as their availability." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a4e5cdca7f5b0b7cab0a9151c06b52a64976acc> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e6784c628e8dc459dadd70756d576de1 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9a4e5cdca7f5b0b7cab0a9151c06b52a64976acc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:e6784c628e8dc459dadd70756d576de1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e6784c628e8dc459dadd70756d576de1 <http://schema.org/value> "London" .
