<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:9747e964207055b2af78cff33822178895209301> <http://schema.org/description> "1. Records of Shad sp. and Allis Shad catches by commercial salmon netsmen (Allis Shad where species identification confirmed from examination by expert); 2. Records of Shad and Allis Shad (Allis Shad where species identification confirmed from examination by expert) caught by rod anglers, angling clubs and commercial salmon and sea trout estuary netsmen; 3. Records of Allis Shad caught and examined at Gunnislake Fish Trap; 4. Records of Shad (presumed Allis Shad as inferred from trap records) counted by Gunnislake Fish Counter and observed on camera footage as they migrate upstream at the tidal limit; 5. Sightings of live Shad; 6. Records of dead Shad carcasses; 7. Records of Shad egg surveys. Egg surveys in estuary or river using a standard long-handled macroinvertebrate kick-sampling net and technique.\r\n The original database is held by the Environment Agency. If you have any questions about data contained within it, contact Robert Hillman (see contacts)." .
_:ee6986c45ecf2d050f094c68e49e37f0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:97475fff27b14bae861564c02ad5c6ba8f7c4a27> <http://schema.org/description> "The report in this series describes the results of botanical surveys carried out in September 2015. It describes the baseline condition of saltmarsh vegetation found along the export cable routes between kilometer point (KP) 0,2 and KP1.2. This baseline survey has been designed to allow a comparison of vegetation structure and composition following export cable installation works, due to commence in May 2016. It also provides a summary of the results of vegetation surveys undertaken in association with the 2014 geotechnical investigation works on the saltmarsh." .
_:de7943712e3d161a214539121b464449 <http://schema.org/value> "saltmarsh vegetation" .
