_:cb2bb15ea90dec0dd732fb76ffcf6bd3 <http://schema.org/value> "cone resistance" .
_:f19da462373e07797f132506aca44b4c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:fbf30d89add21d6cab0380fa613abb3c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:965877b5bc30109ee8591d9b3ba1675b849bb141> <http://schema.org/description> "At the request of Subocean Ltd, a Cone Penetration soil investigation was carried put on Lynn and Inner Dowsing by Lankelma Ltd The tests performed consisted of 11 electric Piezocone Tests (CPTU’s) to a maximum depth of 13.99 or refusal. All tests were performed and measured the cone resistance, local side friction and pore water pressure with depth.\r\n\r\nThe report presented covers the factual reports with estimated soil types." .
_:c502f611f75ff4d7c784e65c2b89d0a7 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:f19da462373e07797f132506aca44b4c <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:c502f611f75ff4d7c784e65c2b89d0a7 <http://schema.org/value> "Subocean Ltd" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:965877b5bc30109ee8591d9b3ba1675b849bb141> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fbf30d89add21d6cab0380fa613abb3c .
_:cb2bb15ea90dec0dd732fb76ffcf6bd3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c502f611f75ff4d7c784e65c2b89d0a7 <http://schema.org/value> "Lankelma Ltd" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:965483bf498c376b0e107401ac210ccff4b64970> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:eb587eb72596541096a6a3e7dcb7a069 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:965483bf498c376b0e107401ac210ccff4b64970> <http://schema.org/description> "In 2005, Greater Gabbard Offshore Winds Limited (GGOWL) submitted an Environmental Statement (ES) for the development of the Greater Gabbard offshore wind farm (GGOWF) 26km offshore of Orford Ness on the Suffolk Coast. The Greater Gabbard Offshore Wind Farm (GGOWF) was formally awarded consent in February 2007. A number of conditions were attached to this consent, one of which relates to the continued ornithological monitoring at the site. This was to build on the baseline work undertaken in 2004 and 2006, in order to assess for impacts from the offshore wind farm on both resident and migratory bird populations. Subsequently, an Ornithological Monitoring Protocol (Protocol) was prepared by GGOWL in order to meet the requirements for monitoring set out in the conditions of Food and Environment Protection Act (FEPA) 1985 licence reference 33097/07/0 (dated 24th July 2007). Environmentally Sustainable Systems Limited (ESS) was commissioned by GGOWL to undertake the ornithological monitoring works for the GGOWF in 2008, with the first of the monthly surveys undertaken in June 2008. In accordance with the FEPA Licence requirements, the monitoring programme will include pre-construction, during construction and post-construction phases of the development. This series covers the pre-construction surveys carried out between June 2008 and May 2009. The monthly survey reports and corresponding datasets are provided, which include counts and density estimates, and track data. In addition, quarterly reports are provided, which summarise the findings of monitoring work for each quarter." .
_:c4cd7bd5a0864219a880b917ec8053d3 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
