<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:907370ee8e8fe58e72db6ddb0063aa11a6012b47> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f6d3778772b1f0d08e5ed0e82cda5c37 .
_:b3f2d9a4e8a16b9873b8fa2fd66d2b99 <http://schema.org/value> "side scan sonar" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:907370ee8e8fe58e72db6ddb0063aa11a6012b47> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:907370ee8e8fe58e72db6ddb0063aa11a6012b47> <http://schema.org/description> "EGS (International) Ltd were contracted by Centrica Renewable Energy Limited (CREL) to carry out a geophysical survey of the Lincs OWF, located offshore of Skegness on the east coast of England. The main objective of the survey was to fulfil the Lincs Operations and Maintenance requirements. High resolution multibeam and side scan sonar was acquired with 100% bathymetric and side scan coverage achieved around all 75 turbines and the 4 substation legs. 100% bathymetric and side scan sonar (200% insonification) coverage was achieved across the array and collector cables as well as each â??No Cable Zoneâ?? within the windfarm in order the assess the extent of any changes to bedform morphology along the route." .
_:b3f2d9a4e8a16b9873b8fa2fd66d2b99 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
