_:fc1dcb9d03d3aa6a8103f54620350365 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8ad4f375f2316fce8a9a41ccb202fb4ec39d17ca> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fc1dcb9d03d3aa6a8103f54620350365 .
_:fc1dcb9d03d3aa6a8103f54620350365 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8ad4f375f2316fce8a9a41ccb202fb4ec39d17ca> <http://schema.org/description> "Report: Arnold, SE. 1971. Cruise Report for MV Moray Firth IV North Irish Sea Survey. MGU Project 69/02. (IGS Report No 17) Positioning: Main Chain Decca with Mark12 receiver Echo Sounding: Kelvin Hughes MS 36 and MS32 Sonar Systems: EG&amp;G side-scan sonar Kelvin Hughes MS43 Mk1 transit sonar Seismic Systems: Sparker System: EG&amp;G sparker system with 16 element hydrophone streamer. Most lines run at either 0.5kJ or 3kJ Magnetometer: Varian magnetometer. See also IGS report 71/19." .
_:b82546e61ad5059514febbcea4393722 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d1f0ba15dda19cfea43ee7dc2043bde0 <http://schema.org/value> "North Irish Sea" .
_:fc1dcb9d03d3aa6a8103f54620350365 <http://schema.org/value> "IGS" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8ad4f375f2316fce8a9a41ccb202fb4ec39d17ca> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d1f0ba15dda19cfea43ee7dc2043bde0 .
_:d1f0ba15dda19cfea43ee7dc2043bde0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8ad4f375f2316fce8a9a41ccb202fb4ec39d17ca> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8acd87656971ac7295a4a18820c2732a4e8b633d> <http://schema.org/description> "Bibby HydroMap were commissioned by Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Ltd/EDF Renewables, in August 2018, to undertake a series of geophysical surveys at the Blyth Offshore Demonstrator wind farm, located off the north-east coast of the UK at Blyth, Northumberland. \r\n The 41.5 MW wind farm is located approximately 6km offshore of Blyth and comprises five wind turbine generators configured in a single row, as indicated in Figure 1 below. Surveys have been previously undertaken in August/September 2018, April 2019, and this, the most recent survey, was undertaken between the 29th October and 20th November 2019.\r\n Due to the general lack of seabed mobility, the survey boundary for this monitoring visit has been reduced to decrease survey acquisition and processing timescales for the client. The new boundaries were submitted to and approved by the Marine Management Organisation (MMO) in October 2019.\r\nThis survey, comprising the collection of multibeam bathymetry and side scan sonar data, marks the third of a 3-year monitoring program, which will be undertaken at 6 monthly intervals, and after any major storm events. \r\nThe objectives of the survey program were to acquire survey data to a resolution that will:\r\nIdentify seabed debris within the construction area; \r\n- Identify changes to seabed morphology to enable the evaluation of the effectiveness of installed scour protection and ratify predictions for scour development; \r\n- Inform the foundation and cable maintenance schedule; \r\n- Satisfy the requirements of the Marine Licence." .
_:f069cd058d054b8c6e9bea10b579e948 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e6395ee71d0e7d3ed5997785da4b3796 <http://schema.org/value> "UK" .
