_:b2bbdd401c66f6e23dc1ed1995239905 <http://schema.org/value> "Ambios Environmental Consultants Ltd." .
_:b61fea885fb639668ba2a19010616821 <http://schema.org/value> "Lyme Bay" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aae6219c248c7b3cde50fbce14b74f1ecb4ab0b> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c8403304ca228d7891a5580b95b8139c .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aae6219c248c7b3cde50fbce14b74f1ecb4ab0b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aae6219c248c7b3cde50fbce14b74f1ecb4ab0b> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b2bbdd401c66f6e23dc1ed1995239905 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aae6219c248c7b3cde50fbce14b74f1ecb4ab0b> <http://schema.org/description> "Survey run by Ambios Environmental Consultants Ltd. for Kerr-McGee Oil (UK) plc. All these records relate to \"Dyrynda, Cleator (1995) - Lyme Bay Environmental Study Volume 5. The Fleet Lagoon\" A copy of the report is held at Dorset Environmental Records Centre.\r\n This report forms part of the 'Lyme Bay Environmental Study' series. This volume focuses on seven sites in the Fleet: two within the tide exposed lagoonal link channel, and a further five within the sheltered lagoonal basin. Dive transects were used at six of these sites to characterise habitats and epibenthic communities, the remain site was sampled as a spot sample. A sinking transect line marked at 2m intervals was deployed cross-channel, from the low tide level of the seaward (Chesil) shore towards land. A maximum length of 260m was used for each transect, which enabled the lagoon width to be spanned at all sites except for Littlesea. A pair of divers swam along the transect line, recording at each 2m interval the water depth and, within a 0.5m radius, the substratum and conspicuous biota. For the lagoonal basin transects, the percentage cover of seagrasses and green algal mats were visually estimated. Species lists for most sites have been compiled from text descriptions as the 'station by species matrix' referred to in the report as 'Table 6' is missing from the report. \r\n NB Grid references relate to the location on the Chesil shore corresponding with the start point of the dive transect." .
_:b2bbdd401c66f6e23dc1ed1995239905 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:a9210b664cbb2522e3cb4a74d0fd73b <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:eec37afb17c4351248f9f449b88ee63 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:bb106d039ae7f5f12ed8dc26707c300e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:aa86f8316ff564a404a19171256a5af2 <http://schema.org/value> "turbulence profiler" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aa371484caf9dd979fe2ccab9b43ec0cdd9cda6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a1e72cda748adab2269a24d454e54297 .
_:aa86f8316ff564a404a19171256a5af2 <http://schema.org/value> "SeaSoar profiler" .
_:aa86f8316ff564a404a19171256a5af2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:bb106d039ae7f5f12ed8dc26707c300e <http://schema.org/value> "National Oceanography Centre" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8aa371484caf9dd979fe2ccab9b43ec0cdd9cda6> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset consists of a variety of hydrographic, biological, biogeochemical and meteorological data. Underway automatic sampling followed by flow cytometry was used for assessing mesoscale spatial variability of microorganisms. Coarse-scale (CTD) and fine-scale (PumpCast profiler) vertical distribution of microorganisms was determined, with dominant microbial prokaryotic and eukaryotic groups quantified by flow cytometry. Samples were collected and processed for subsequent molecular identification of flow cytometrically sorted dominant microbes. Abundance of larger microplankton organisms was assessed. Microbial respiration in the twilight zone was studied. Group-specific uptake of bicarbonate, phosphate and different nitrogen compounds was determined and group-specific production and grazing assessed using flow sorting. The ambient turnover rates of phosphate, organic phosphorus and labile dissolved organic matter, e.g. amino acids, was bioassayed. In order to put the microbial community data into context, physical and chemical parameters were measured. A ship mounted Acoustic Doppler Current Profiler (ADCP) was used to collect information about physical, mesoscale spatial context and, when combined with turbulence profiler data, SeaSoar profiler data and data collected using intensive Conductivity, Temperature and Depth (CTD) sampling for dissolved inorganic nutrients, may estimate mesoscale nutrient fluxes into the photic zone. PELAGRA neutral buoyancy sediment traps were used to estimate biogenic sedimentation. Samples were collected for particulate calcite, opal, and Particulate Organic Matter (POM) measurements, together with the isotopic composition of Particulate Organic Nitrogen (PON). Data collection was in the North Atlantic subtropical gyre between 9th August and 15th September 2011 during RRS Discovery cruise D369. The data were collected as part of the United Kingdom (UK) Natural Environment Research Council (NERC) Oceans 2025 programme (Theme 2). D369 was the last of three National Oceanography Centre 'process study' research cruises to be run by the Ocean Biogeochemistry and Ecosystems research group under the NERC Ocean 2025 research programme. The Principal Scientist was Mikhail V Zubkov of National Oceanography Centre, Southampton. Data from this cruise are held at the British Oceanographic Data Centre." .
