<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a12cf217096d9d065d5b0b60400577a2747b1f1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b7ce504614bb4e54c6c4a9fd1b4d9bee .
_:b7ce504614bb4e54c6c4a9fd1b4d9bee <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b7ce504614bb4e54c6c4a9fd1b4d9bee <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:a38b990646e88801bf598ccfa50cda24 <http://schema.org/value> "depths" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a12cf217096d9d065d5b0b60400577a2747b1f1> <http://schema.org/description> "Geosurv offered to review existing sub-bottom profiler data (boomer) gathered by Osiris Ltd. during their survey campaign between 4th and 8th May 2010. The purpose of the investigation was twofold: \r\n1) To see whether the boomer penetrated sufficiently into the seabed for foundation design purposes \r\n2) If subsequent sub-bottom data was to be acquired what instrument would be suitable for the task.\r\n\r\nThe boomer sub-bottom data files were played back through Coda replay and the lowest depth reflector mapped. All lines were reviewed (a total of 13 files) together with a brief replay of the side scan sonar data The Sub-bottom data was exported from Coda and imported into ArcGIS for review against Osiris multibeam image of the seabed. The depths picked for rockhead could then be compared to the sea floor features, in particular areas of bedrock and or sub-rock (bedrock close to but not actually outcropping on the seafloor i.e. a veneer of sediment overlies the rock)." .
_:a38b990646e88801bf598ccfa50cda24 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:b7ce504614bb4e54c6c4a9fd1b4d9bee <http://schema.org/value> "Osiris Ltd." .
_:a568da37242bf0dd8b2344e2719cd824 <http://schema.org/value> "Ireland Trough" .
_:b5f296aa76f8c4a50e442ff9bf80b96c <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:a568da37242bf0dd8b2344e2719cd824 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:a568da37242bf0dd8b2344e2719cd824 <http://schema.org/value> "North East Atlantic Ocean" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a0cd662c8589b5f6f6493a7c43ccf155a8b1ab3> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b5f296aa76f8c4a50e442ff9bf80b96c .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a0cd662c8589b5f6f6493a7c43ccf155a8b1ab3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a0cd662c8589b5f6f6493a7c43ccf155a8b1ab3> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 2 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the North East Atlantic Ocean (limit 40W) area specifically at the Ireland Trough and the Porcupine Seabight, from August to October of 1979. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Institute of Oceanographic Sciences Wormley Laboratory." .
_:a568da37242bf0dd8b2344e2719cd824 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b5f296aa76f8c4a50e442ff9bf80b96c <http://schema.org/value> "Institute of Oceanographic Sciences Wormley Laboratory" .
_:b5f296aa76f8c4a50e442ff9bf80b96c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
