_:b8a6455a5c1c651de789e69c012e03ed <http://schema.org/value> "Western Irish Margin" .
_:b8a6455a5c1c651de789e69c012e03ed <http://schema.org/value> "Rockall Trough" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a0a344062eac72e031a0e257aa5116eb7689a49> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b8a6455a5c1c651de789e69c012e03ed .
_:b8a6455a5c1c651de789e69c012e03ed <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cf244929008c3e6dfe0aaf49b079bb1 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
_:b8a6455a5c1c651de789e69c012e03ed <http://schema.org/value> "Barra Fan" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a0a344062eac72e031a0e257aa5116eb7689a49> <http://schema.org/description> "This collaborative marine sampling survey took place in June 2004 in the areas of the Goban Spur, Western Irish Margin, Barra Fan and Rosemary Bank onboard the R/V Marion Dufresne. The British Geological Survey (BGS) participation centred around the collection of one long sediment core in the Barra Fan, Rockall Trough. The objective was to obtain a high resolution sedimentary record for the comparison of at least 4 major glacial cycles extending possibly into the early Pleistocene. Equipment used: CALYPSO Giant Piston Core - one 37.7m core collected. Technical details of the survey are contained in BGS Report IR/04/126 (http://nora.nerc.ac.uk/id/eprint/509377/). Publication with core details see NORA http://nora.nerc.ac.uk/9636/." .
_:cf244929008c3e6dfe0aaf49b079bb1 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:8a0a344062eac72e031a0e257aa5116eb7689a49> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
