<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88f63ca94e119a891dce39c34657f83c5e031430> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 14 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, taken from the Irish Sea and St. George's Channel area specifically SW of the Isle of Man and NW of Holyhead Island, during September 1981. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the University of Wales, Bangor School of Ocean Sciences." .
_:e471a0721bf230bb00b8a578570c49b5 <http://schema.org/value> "Tiree" .
_:e471a0721bf230bb00b8a578570c49b5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e471a0721bf230bb00b8a578570c49b5 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88f637934f897586e0bbeb4ad15bda7acada5db6> <http://schema.org/description> "ScottishPower Renewables (UK) Ltd (SPR) is proposing to develop a wind farm, named Argyll Array, located in the vicinity of Tiree, Scottish Inner Hebrides. In order to determine the safe construction, operation, and decommissioning of the proposed development, an assessment of vessel navigation is required. The assessment will include collecting and analysing data on shipping passing within and in the vicinity of the proposed wind farm site. SPR commissioned Marine &amp; Risk Consultants Limited (Marico Marine) to provide a qualified and experienced marine consultant to lead the impact assessment of the proposed site with respect to shipping and navigation." .
_:e471a0721bf230bb00b8a578570c49b5 <http://schema.org/value> "Scottish Inner Hebrides" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:88f637934f897586e0bbeb4ad15bda7acada5db6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e471a0721bf230bb00b8a578570c49b5 .
