<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:87156b976399bed1224ce05593d6967270fdcfa3> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:cdff82e7bbcf5f9babab5a8e964ac4e0 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:87156b976399bed1224ce05593d6967270fdcfa3> <http://schema.org/description> "Osiris Projects were commissioned by DONG Energy to carry out a detailed\r\nhydrographic and geophysical survey at the Burbo Bank offshore wind farm\r\ndevelopment, together with an associated cable route and two separate transit routes.\r\nData acquisition was undertaken by Osiris Projects using Ocean Marines custom-built\r\nshallow-drafted vessel, MV 'Barinthus'. The vessel was equipped with single beam\r\necho sounder, side scan sonar, and marine magnetometer systems. Vessel\r\npositioning during the survey was provided by the use of CSI Vector Sensor DGPS.\r\nThe vessel was mobilised at Conwy, N Wales, and was subsequently based in Canada\r\nDock, Liverpool for the duration of survey operations. This gave a transit time to site of\r\napproximately 20 minutes.\r\nDue to the large number of charts produced, the report is split into two volumes. Volume 1 contains an interpretation of the individual data sets, including the charts from the development area and its associated cable route, together with details of the operational parameters, locations, times and techniques utilised during the surveys. Volume 2 contains the alignment charts for the two transit routes only." .
_:c95831048fda9aa95418d75d4fd66ef4 <http://schema.org/value> "Osiris Projects" .
_:f941f6ea17fd955db310d70545e5f6cb <http://schema.org/value> "DONG Energy" .
