<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7f356ed41d4e8ac47b29ae18cd5c431199209a13> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d8bac813dc365bf6b168f1fdd2048073 .
_:d8bac813dc365bf6b168f1fdd2048073 <http://schema.org/value> "Orford Ness" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7f356ed41d4e8ac47b29ae18cd5c431199209a13> <http://schema.org/description> "Bird survey monitoring reports produced during the construction phase of the Greater Gabbard Offshore Wind Farm.In 2005, Greater Gabbard Offshore Winds Limited (GGOWL) submitted an Environmental Statement (ES) for the development of the Greater Gabbard Offshore Wind Farm (GGOWF) 26km offshore of Orford Ness on the Suffolk Coast. The GGOWF was formally awarded consent in February 2007. A number of conditions were attached to this consent, one of which relates to the continued ornithological monitoring at the site. This was to build on the baseline work undertaken in 2004 and 2006, in order to assess for impacts from the offshore wind farm on both resident and migratory bird populations. Subsequently, an Ornithological Monitoring Protocol was prepared by GGOWL in order to meet the requirements for monitoring set out in the conditions of Food and Environment Protection Act (FEPA) 1985 licence reference 33097/07/0 (dated 24th July 2007). Environmentally Sustainable Systems Limited (ESS) was commissioned by GGOWL to undertake the ornithological monitoring works for the GGOWF in 2008, with the first of the monthly surveys undertaken in June 2008. In accordance with the FEPA Licence requirements, the monitoring programme will include pre-construction, during construction and post-construction phases of the development. This series covers the construction surveys carried out between June 2010 and May 2011. The monthly survey reports and corresponding datasets are provided, which include counts and density estimates, and track data. In addition, quarterly reports are provided, which summarise the findings of monitoring work for each quarter." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7f356ed41d4e8ac47b29ae18cd5c431199209a13> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:de78709c11cc52474d4fb2fdc906c392 .
_:de78709c11cc52474d4fb2fdc906c392 <http://schema.org/value> "Environmentally Sustainable Systems Limited" .
_:de78709c11cc52474d4fb2fdc906c392 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:f8e80b34660cd54b960433e359041d42 <http://schema.org/name> "policies" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7f3552f95cba311e1a1bfb1c323d39ee777eb742> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ada2f8bfe3afd1450b8c17c1e01aa782 .
_:ada2f8bfe3afd1450b8c17c1e01aa782 <http://schema.org/value> "Navitus Bay\r\nDevelopment Limited" .
_:ada2f8bfe3afd1450b8c17c1e01aa782 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7f3552f95cba311e1a1bfb1c323d39ee777eb742> <http://schema.org/description> "Coastline Surveys Ltd (CSL) was commissioned by PMSS on behalf of Navitus Bay\r\nDevelopment Limited (NBDL) to undertake a marine geotechnical site investigation for the\r\nNavitus Bay Development area. The aim was to obtain information on the geotechnical\r\ncharacteristics of the sediment along a section of the development area and cable route corridor.\r\nThis was necessary to inform archaeological assessment of the sediment as well as providing\r\ngeological and geotechnical information for the cable engineering design for the proposed Navitus\r\nBay Wind Park. A Vibrocore (VC) survey campaign involving 22no x 6m VC at locations supplied\r\nby PMSS (client rep) has been completed by CSL onboard Coastline’s dedicated survey vessel\r\n“MV FlatHolm”. The vibrocore survey was carried out between February 27th and March\r\n1st 2013 using the CSL C-CoreHP High Penetration Corer." .
_:ada2f8bfe3afd1450b8c17c1e01aa782 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ada2f8bfe3afd1450b8c17c1e01aa782 <http://schema.org/value> "PMSS" .
