<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d71cbbe733ff95fc41c56c0eecce8dd11f58263> <http://schema.org/description> "Samples and associated geological data are held at the British Geological Survey for Maritime Coastguard Agency (MCA), Civil Hydrography Programme (CHP), Bathymetric Survey HI1292; East Anglia Routine Resurvey, East Anglia Routine Resurvey Block 3, Area in SqKm: 20; East Anglia Routine Resurvey Block 1, Area in SqKm: 0; East Anglia Routine Resurvey Block 2, Area in SqKm: 1, (17/07/2009 to 10/08/2009), Standard: IHO S44ed5 Order 1a. Contract: RRS (2006 LT). FY 2008/09. Contractor: MMT." .
_:bf98d152a7d1cbd3f795d38f9c89801b <http://schema.org/value> "greater Severn estuary" .
_:bf98d152a7d1cbd3f795d38f9c89801b <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:bf98d152a7d1cbd3f795d38f9c89801b <http://schema.org/value> "Bristol Channel" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d5dd0a55e8aeabed2ebdd64b7ba1c8d9f6351a3> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bf98d152a7d1cbd3f795d38f9c89801b .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d5dd0a55e8aeabed2ebdd64b7ba1c8d9f6351a3> <http://schema.org/description> "The study aimed to assess and map the delivery of key ecosystem services (ES) within the greater Severn estuary and Bristol Channel. The project aimed to provide a tool for stakeholders, regulators and the marine renewable industry to support decision making in the region. Identification of hotspots for key ES was intended to provide developers with an insight into locations with a high consenting risk." .
_:bf98d152a7d1cbd3f795d38f9c89801b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d5dd0a55e8aeabed2ebdd64b7ba1c8d9f6351a3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7d5895780ea4809a5ce35b16c64cde37dd8f0c88> <http://schema.org/description> "Ad-hoc series of dives in Torbay area all carried out in 2007 using Seasearch methodology. As of 16/10/07, survey comprises of 7 Seasearch Observation forms. Data on species and biotope recorded and entered onto Marine Recorder. Species data and biotope data mapped as points using MapInfo." .
