_:f6c068e7f1e5ca17f3519d9c51757e51 <http://schema.org/value> "Scotland" .
_:d5914756d544cea0ecc9a82801e7a4f5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d5914756d544cea0ecc9a82801e7a4f5 <http://schema.org/value> "hydrographic data profiles" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7ce22e81cf3d8ad35a0d25c0943d6f57d6eea382> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 67 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the Irish Sea and St. George's Channel area specifically the north and west coasts of Scotland and Irish Sea during March 2005. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Fisheries Research Services Aberdeen Marine Laboratory." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7ce22e81cf3d8ad35a0d25c0943d6f57d6eea382> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7cce9c523a901c7f353041b6235c097d30b09ab7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:b81c3edddcaecfb8d6881a91137afd07 <http://schema.org/value> "Essex tidal estuaries" .
_:b81c3edddcaecfb8d6881a91137afd07 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7cce9c523a901c7f353041b6235c097d30b09ab7> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e655d47ff26383f4b494ca1843b980c0 .
_:e655d47ff26383f4b494ca1843b980c0 <http://schema.org/name> "migratory marine species" .
_:e655d47ff26383f4b494ca1843b980c0 <http://schema.org/value> "fish" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7cce9c523a901c7f353041b6235c097d30b09ab7> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b81c3edddcaecfb8d6881a91137afd07 .
_:e655d47ff26383f4b494ca1843b980c0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7cce9c523a901c7f353041b6235c097d30b09ab7> <http://schema.org/description> "The Essex tidal estuaries are the site of a number of timber-built fish traps, their distribution being particularly dense in the Blackwater estuary where six sites have been identified through the work of local archaeologists and aerial reconnaissance. The Blackwater examples are Saxon in date (Strachan 1998) and comprise large and complex monuments, comprising numerous wooden posts in various alignments, along with wattle-work (sails and rods) and basketry. The recovered information adds to the understanding of these and other fishtraps in the Blackwater estuary and provides measurable data with which to assess the nature and rate of erosion taking place in this inter-tidal environment. Additionally, a number of methodological lessons have been learnt that are of benefit to the improved investigation of such monuments in the inter-tidal zone." .
_:b81c3edddcaecfb8d6881a91137afd07 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b81c3edddcaecfb8d6881a91137afd07 <http://schema.org/value> "Blackwater estuary" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7cc544d18422486bad06114da831a076b9c447e1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ccefc8aea41448a7500563f13a7205c8 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7cc544d18422486bad06114da831a076b9c447e1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:de1629f68787528860aa502fc7098f7 .
_:ccefc8aea41448a7500563f13a7205c8 <http://schema.org/value> "Barrow-in-Furness" .
_:d6aac19f7af32ae9864a593e25f975ec <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:d6aac19f7af32ae9864a593e25f975ec <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:de1629f68787528860aa502fc7098f7 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ccefc8aea41448a7500563f13a7205c8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ccefc8aea41448a7500563f13a7205c8 <http://schema.org/value> "Irish Sea" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7cc544d18422486bad06114da831a076b9c447e1> <http://schema.org/description> "An archaeological assessment of geophysical data as part of evaluation works for the Ormonde Offshore Windfarm and associated export cable route. The site lies within the eastern Irish Sea off Barrow-in-Furness, with the cable route coming ashore near Heysham. The geophysical data consisted of sidescan sonar, sub-bottom profiler and magnetometer data, which were acquired by Gardline Geosurvey Limited in 2004 and 2008." .
_:d6aac19f7af32ae9864a593e25f975ec <http://schema.org/value> "sub-bottom profiler" .
_:ccefc8aea41448a7500563f13a7205c8 <http://schema.org/value> "Heysham" .
_:de1629f68787528860aa502fc7098f7 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
