<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7946deb841ce6fbcd39026caca4e1fc76832cc17> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f43e63186643e8d28bfbb757ef755b2e .
_:e4344362790804595f5dd135e7e704cb <http://schema.org/value> "Blyth" .
_:f8fee2e32a004b2f368d06a80398c907 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:793f65bb3ff2c344bef46f3384e67b160ec5c2f7> <http://schema.org/description> "Bibby HydroMap were commissioned by Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Ltd/EDF Renewables, in August 2018, to undertake two geophysical surveys (in August-September 2018 and April 2019) at the Blyth Offshore Demonstrator wind farm, located off the north-east coast of the UK at Blyth, Northumberland.\r\n The 41.5 MW wind farm is located approximately 6km offshore of Blyth and comprises five wind turbine generators configured in a single row. The 2019 survey was undertaken between 16th and 30th April 2019.\r\n This survey, comprising the collection of multibeam bathymetry and side scan sonar data, marks the first of a 3-year monitoring program, which will be undertaken at 6 monthly intervals, and after any major storm events.\r\n The objectives of the survey program are to acquire survey data to a resolution that will:\r\n - Identify seabed debris within the construction area;\r\n - Identify changes to seabed morphology, to enable the evaluation of the effectiveness of installed scour protection and ratify predictions for scour development;\r\n - Inform the foundation and cable maintenance schedule; and\r\n - Satisfy the requirements of the Marine Licence." .
_:e4344362790804595f5dd135e7e704cb <http://schema.org/value> "UK" .
_:f8fee2e32a004b2f368d06a80398c907 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Licence" .
