<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:7902ecc4aea36135f24c65faf96b2e55c94f6cc6> <http://schema.org/description> "The South Coast Regional Environmental Characterisation study is a multidisciplinery project involving the biology, geology and archaeology of an area of the English Channel 5800km2. Funded by the MALSF. A 2m scientific beam trawl with a 5mm mesh liner was used to sample epibenthic fauna. Benthic samples were collected for faunal and granulometric analysis using a 0.1m2 Hamon Grab." .
