<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:76ecf1593649f82f64f4d65e7a045491365c41bf> <http://schema.org/description> "This geophysical survey has been carried out by British Geological Survey (BGS), the survey took place in December 1990 in the Irish Sea on board the RRS Charles Darwin. The purpose was to collect gravity data as part of the UK continental shelf survey programme at the start of a University of Cambridge cruise. Sea floor data were collected using echo sounder. Gravity and magnetic data were acquired. These data are archived by BGS. BGS Survey mentioned in University of Cambridge OCEAN site survey cruise (CD54/90) report on BODC website. No BGS survey report currently available." .
_:a41b2b317306fd22ed5c30162a99f335 <http://schema.org/value> "University of Cambridge" .
