_:efdf6ce71b60dbcbce1090c4979ab4fc <http://schema.org/value> "Lynn" .
_:e5dfc4e10e562d7f140d329746516371 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:75434245a3151d5bf9d50539b5311e947b6a2d40> <http://schema.org/description> "In fulfilment of its FEPA license requirements ongoing monitoring is being carried out covering the two wind farm sites (Inner Dowsing and Lynn) and a control site. This project relates to the surveys carried out from July – December 2007. Eight surveys were undertaken using transects to sample bird numbers and distribution on the water and in flight. The outcomes of the survey show that red-throated divers continue only to be recorded in low density at distances greater than 5km offshore as well as common scoter. Auks were recorded in great numbers within the Lynn site during construction. The recommendations are for a continuation of boat-based monitoring throughout 2008 and monitoring of different bird species ongoing use of turbine bases." .
_:e29eccbddc4aa15296307c101f84596d <http://schema.org/value> "RSKENSR Environment Limited" .
_:d122a17532aa7797743a7b1348bde3a6 <http://schema.org/value> "Heysham" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:75414ecc828411e77229df05dbda03cb05a35c95> <http://schema.org/description> "On the instructions of RSKENSR Environment Limited, Osiris Projects were commissioned to carry out a pre-construction survey covering the proposed Barrow Offshore Wind Farm development site and associated cable and navigation routes. The main development site survey covered an area of approximately 9.8km².\r\nHigh-resolution side scan sonar and single beam bathymetry data were acquired along all survey lines, which were run at 100m centres, with cross lines at 500m centres, in order to accurately map the entire seabed within the wind farm development area. For the proposed cable route into Heysham, two parallel survey lines were run at 100m separation. For the navigation route into Barrow-in-Furness, four survey lines were run at 50m separation.\r\nData acquisition took place during the period 29th March to 2nd April 2005, with survey works undertaken using the survey vessel MV ‘Lia’. \r\nThe primary objective of the survey was to map seabed features and bathymetry within the wind farm area and along the associated cable and navigation routes, in order to establish the presence of any debris. This data will be used as ‘baseline’ information for comparison with further survey data, which will be collected after construction of the turbines and associated cabling has been completed." .
_:e29eccbddc4aa15296307c101f84596d <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
