<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:74d8216e45437cd31095f802148a563f6e676853> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d8668acca4cbf0e69c0d11f1c3a1e0b6 .
_:fd6043231b039a882e02951518bdf794 <http://schema.org/value> "DONG Energy" .
_:eed8524a3523a2a0a80f8e6e45c9fc9e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f259fece96039325d3c7997e34b331cb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:74cdfc5b9f0fa17dcc234b8b3db60e8a8b8c4b55> <http://schema.org/description> "Fugro EMU Limited was commissioned by DONG Energy to undertake an unexploded ordnance (UXO) and environmental engineering survey for the Race Bank Offshore Wind Farm (ROW01). The survey area was located in the Wash area off the Norfolk coast, UK. Acquisition of multibeam bathymetry, sidescan sonar and magnetometer data was carried out along the intended export cable routes, inter-array cable routes and on any required wind turbine generator sites. The majority of the offshore survey area was divided between the RV Discovery and the Victor Hensen, with shallow survey operations conducted by the Fugro Seeker. Vessel mobilisations began on the week of the 23 February 2015 in Great Yarmouth, UK, whereupon calibrations and UXO acceptance tests were carried out. Survey operations commenced on the 4 and 5 March 2015 and were completed by the 20 and 16 April 2015 by the RV Discovery and Victor Hensen, respectively. This was followed by a two day demobilisation for each vessel. The inshore extent of survey operations were conducted on board the Fugro Seeker and completed on 27 April 2015." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:74cdfc5b9f0fa17dcc234b8b3db60e8a8b8c4b55> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fd6043231b039a882e02951518bdf794 .
