_:dd8c0772f7d801c7adc3b57019967316 <http://schema.org/name> "policies" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72b2cb0b07f0e4863a08c9782a44226bb29eda55> <http://schema.org/description> "Operations and maintenance geophysical survey for Teesside Offshore Wind Farm between 26 March 2014 and 5 April 2014. \r\nThe aims of the survey were to: To identify debris within the construction area; To identify changes to seabed morphology, to enable the evaluation of the\r\neffectiveness of installed scour protection and ratify the predictions for scour\r\ndevelopment; To Inform the foundation and cable maintenance schedule; To satisfy the requirements of the Marine License, specifically the monitoring of\r\nArchaeological Exclusion Zones." .
_:fe7f9b208c1a048548de8c7025960939 <http://schema.org/value> "Cornwall Council" .
_:ba6a729f62a6c4bb471886bcbe77dd6 <http://schema.org/value> "Historic Environment Projects" .
_:fe7f9b208c1a048548de8c7025960939 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:fe7f9b208c1a048548de8c7025960939 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72aca7179c56707085966035519e03f1cacb7a49> <http://schema.org/description> "In March 2009 English Heritage commissioned Historic Environment Projects, Cornwall Council to carry out an initial theoretical study to result in an Updated Project Design (UPD) to inform field trials of different types of marine magnetometer in controlled conditions. The project was funded through the Aggregates Levy Sustainability Fund (ALSF). The main part of the theoretical study was carried out by a team of external maritime and/or geophysics specialists." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:72aca7179c56707085966035519e03f1cacb7a49> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fe7f9b208c1a048548de8c7025960939 .
