<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:705148f58497c6dfa404b288bab081f830b9d3ac> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d4da6e21a792be72e31802ff2624610c .
_:b911597e7b1056a16d6c1276dee9f375 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:d4da6e21a792be72e31802ff2624610c <http://schema.org/value> "Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Ltd (BODL)" .
_:d4da6e21a792be72e31802ff2624610c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d4da6e21a792be72e31802ff2624610c <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:705148f58497c6dfa404b288bab081f830b9d3ac> <http://schema.org/description> "EGS (International) Ltd carried out a survey for Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Ltd (BODL), offshore of\r\nBlyth, northeast England. The objectives of the geophysical survey were to acquire data over Array 2\r\ndredge dump area and 250m radius on 5 WTG locations.\r\nGeophysical operations were undertaken using multibeam echosounder (MBES) and side scan sonar\r\n(SSS) equipment.\r\nThe MBES survey was conducted onboard the EGS Watchful, operating out of the Port of Blyth. The\r\nvessel mobilised on 25th May 2017, with MBES operations completed by 28th May 2017. Due to a fault\r\nwith the vessel’s port engine, SSS acquisition could not be carried out safely so a local vessel of\r\nopportunity (MTS Taktow) was utilised. The vessel was mobilised alongside Blyth on 30th May 2017,\r\nwith acquisition completed on 31st May 2017." .
_:b911597e7b1056a16d6c1276dee9f375 <http://schema.org/value> "Blyth" .
