<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6f16444d4711243a9ce1d4ebebd3e90ee6f838e5> <http://schema.org/description> "Phase 1 of the construction of an offshore wind farm situated midway between the Kent and Essex coastlines and more than 20km from each shore. Phase 1 comprises 175 turbines, 2 offshore substations, and 4 export cables to the shore. This particular part of the project is the archaeological assessment of organic material recovered from 10 Otter and Beam Trawl fish surveys taking place from the 10th to 13th April 2014 as part of post-construction environmental monitoring around the wind farm and and recorded under the London Array Protocol for Archaeological Discoveries managed by the London Array Retained Archaeologist's." .
