<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e7dff1b6a9685baab454d0f1bc504ba1aff3bb0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ef276104527439349251dbf36a085471 <http://schema.org/value> "Osiris Projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e7dff1b6a9685baab454d0f1bc504ba1aff3bb0> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ef276104527439349251dbf36a085471 .
_:ef276104527439349251dbf36a085471 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ef276104527439349251dbf36a085471 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e7dff1b6a9685baab454d0f1bc504ba1aff3bb0> <http://schema.org/description> "Osiris Projects were commissioned by E.ON Climate &amp; Renewables UK to carry out a\r\ndetailed hydrographic and geophysical survey for the Humber Gateway ‘Round Two’\r\noffshore wind farm development area and its associated export cable routes.\r\nSurvey data were acquired across the footprint of the main development site and the\r\ntwo, 1km-wide export cable route corridors (indicated below), the survey extents of\r\nwhich were provided by the Client.\r\naddition, survey data were also acquired at a number of 100m x 100m boxes, which\r\nwere centrally positioned at proposed borehole locations and orientated NNW to SSE\r\nto minimise the effects of any tidal currents on line keeping.\r\nThese additional boxes were undertaken to provide information as to potential UXO\r\nrisk to Contractors and for jack-up rig leg penetration/support calculations." .
_:f2f9f638624e660f3e5d07d514a1af4c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e62a635c5d190676d65b97d686ea60866d6599f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:a62d8ffbbdba7137de1a256b56e5e2bc <http://schema.org/value> "Faroes Fisheries Laboratory" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6e62a635c5d190676d65b97d686ea60866d6599f> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 14 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the Norwegian Sea and the North East Atlantic Ocean (limit 40W) areas specifically in Faroese waters during May 2001. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Faroes Fisheries Laboratory as part of the Monitoring the Atlantic Inflow toward the Arctic (MAIA) project." .
