<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:668f5d04faaeccf3c75b75c6e373ea93228557fe> <http://schema.org/description> "Survey run by Ambios Environmental Consultants Ltd. for Kerr-McGee Oil (UK) plc. All these records relate to \"Rostron, Little (1995) - Lyme Bay Environmental Study Volume 6. Intertidal benthic ecology: Rocky shores\" Copy of the report is held at Dorset Environmental Records Centre.\r\n This report forms part of the 'Lyme Bay Environmental Study' series. This volume aimed to provide an assessment of the ecology of a range of rocky shore types in Lyme Bay. Field survey, using MNCR methodology, took place during spring tide periods of May (23rd-28th) and June (22nd - 27th) 1994. 12 sites in Dorset were surveyed (18 sites surveyed overall, 6 were in Devon) - only the Dorset sites have been entered onto the Dorset database. Numerous site photographs appear throughout report." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:668f5d04faaeccf3c75b75c6e373ea93228557fe> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e8cc8f35dc39d0950df38c428e4baeff .
_:b48b22b4c64cad76d4a29e14f9058eb1 <http://schema.org/value> "Lyme Bay" .
_:f7ce70e8733fa1c5ec37f295b79cc34 <http://schema.org/value> "Wessex Archaeology" .
_:f7ce70e8733fa1c5ec37f295b79cc34 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:668efbd882128b435187ef9b0c794b15cf0bcf48> <http://schema.org/description> "This project was produced by Centrica’s archaeological consultants, Wessex Archaeology, in April 2007. Wessex Archaeology was commissioned to undertake an archaeological assessment upon the potential impact on archaeological remains from the proposed cable route for the Lincs, Docking Shoal and Race Bank Offshore Wind Farms, passing through the Wash. The study included a review of known archaeological sites in the area, and the assessment of geophysical data to identify anomalies which could be of potential archaeological interest. It was included as an Appendix to the Docking Shoal Environmental Statement, published in December 2008. The purpose of the Wash cable route corridor archaeological assessment was to identify potential impacts of the Lincs, Docking Shoal and Race Bank Offshore Wind Farms’ cable corridor on the archaeological environment of the Wash" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:668efbd882128b435187ef9b0c794b15cf0bcf48> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
