<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:64172f115897b021784c62181e0211013e2b4e14> <http://schema.org/description> "This British Geological Survey (BGS) regional sampling survey (comprised of two legs) took place in September/October 1980 in North Sea and the Minch on board the MV Mariner. Four seabed boreholes were drilled using Christensen equipment. These data are archived by BGS. Technical details of the survey are contained in BGS Internal Reports 80/12 &amp; 15." .
