<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:638d467c909d33612f1f1c31bac8a5c500aa959c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:638d467c909d33612f1f1c31bac8a5c500aa959c> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned to undertake an archaeological assessment of geophysical survey data as part of the heritage annual monitoring process for aggregate extraction Areas 473/2. A total of 15 anomalies of archaeological potential have been identified across the Study Area. Three of the anomalies identified have been discriminated as of anthropogenic origin of archaeological interest." .
_:e1498e85567fb48f569ee39282ff1f55 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c38475ffeeb8d7459ea2817a8c463c5e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:63805790f0500d2f0d88784d1d9a80859a2f40d0> <http://schema.org/description> "Intertidal sediment infauna and epibiota species abundance data and associated habitat descriptors from a baseline survey of the Tong Saltings SSSI. The main aims of the survey were to provide sufficient information for site condition assessment and as a baseline for future site condition monitoring. Species abundance data and habitat data was collected in-situ." .
