<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:6209362797e0ded06826b7e4152960f0f7c276d5> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e6df374b60a9adc69d4f847784c70531 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:61ee51e4afa75817347e6c51bdef8308496b6db1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:eadeb76706c684b65445fff2ccd373b8 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:61ee51e4afa75817347e6c51bdef8308496b6db1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:eadeb76706c684b65445fff2ccd373b8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:61ee51e4afa75817347e6c51bdef8308496b6db1> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n \r\n This feature class records the number of people involved in bird watching, mammal watching or botany. Total number of people per annum is recorded by the GroupN field the count field records the number of interviews that contributed to this data.\r\n Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
_:eadeb76706c684b65445fff2ccd373b8 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:eadeb76706c684b65445fff2ccd373b8 <http://schema.org/value> "Stakmap/Fishermap" .
_:e7f243d9a467a0f76c80d6d1f1ccc6ce <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
