<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5fe6341a3c1ce2e66ce1508d7f656aa4858ff7b6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d2cb105658103d2b5aa7da83c6dd57f0 .
_:ca5455ed308557855ca802c18de2bee8 <http://schema.org/value> "Iberian Peninsula" .
_:ca5455ed308557855ca802c18de2bee8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5fe6341a3c1ce2e66ce1508d7f656aa4858ff7b6> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises 61 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, in June 1997 from stations off the coast of the Iberian Peninsula. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Vrije Universiteit Brussels Department of Analytical and Environmental Chemistry as part of the Ocean Margin Exchange (OMEX) II project." .
_:d720dd290a773426a788194e650cda4 <http://schema.org/value> "chlorophyll" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5fdbb6c7fd28bc649cfa4b56a7a1c91a9b5f1038> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset consists of near real-time ocean observations from an autonomous underwater glider, sampling at the Joint North Sea Information System (JONSIS) hydrographic section (2.23°W to 0° at 59.28°N) between 12th October and 2nd December 2013. The measurements were made by a Seaglider (serial number 502) and consist of full-depth temperature, salinity, oxygen, chlorophyll and optical backscatter observations. Dive-average current observations were also collected. This dataset contains standard raw NetCDF (.nc), engineering (.eng) and log (.log) files captured using Seaglider base station version V2.05. The glider deployment was a collaborative effort between the University of East Anglia (UEA) and Marine Scotland Science. Deployment took place from Research Ship MRV Scotia, whilst recovery utilised MPV Jura. The JONSIS repeat section crosses the path of the Fair Isle Current and the East Shetland Atlantic Inflows, key routes by which Atlantic water enters the northern North Sea." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5fdbb6c7fd28bc649cfa4b56a7a1c91a9b5f1038> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d991708fc35448b853e0479f47cc43cd .
