_:da98ee7e6cde8b5e686a710e9413653 <http://schema.org/value> "Shetland Islands" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5f94ba5c4b9e2d55b36a9b3e8ce2bc206c891100> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 3 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the North Sea area specifically around the Shetland Islands, during October of 2005. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Fisheries Research Services Aberdeen Marine Laboratory." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5f8be61a58ab1d81b107c2636597e5eaf7544534> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bac6930c0ea05204db64895010ad0f68 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5f8be61a58ab1d81b107c2636597e5eaf7544534> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e707afc48995481e7c581a4bdc915886 .
_:e707afc48995481e7c581a4bdc915886 <http://schema.org/value> "Flamborough Headland" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5f8be61a58ab1d81b107c2636597e5eaf7544534> <http://schema.org/description> "Report following the survey of chalk shores in North Norfolk and around Flamborough Headland (North Humberside). The survey was part of an on-going review of marine chalk exposures around the British Coast and assesses the nature conservation inmportance of the sites compared with other chalk shores.\r\n The report looks at each survey site one at a time giving a physical description and details of both the fauna and flora present. In addition, species lists and zones (in which they were found) for each are provided. The discussion again looks at the fauna and flora present at the North Norfolk and Flamborough Headland sites. Finally, the nature conservation importance and recommendations are made." .
