<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5dd7eb4935e5c7626c91f89e4e026ab56506c3ba> <http://schema.org/description> "This marine sampling survey took place in October 2002 in the River Clyde between the Lower Harbour and Milton (outer estuary) on board the Endrick 2. The British Geological Survey (BGS) carried out the survey on behalf of Glasgow City Council. The aim was to investigate estuarine geochemistry. Seabed samples were collected using Gravity corer, Mackereth corer and Day grab. Technical details of the survey are contained in BGS Report CR/04/057R." .
