<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5574a11134d33d66e3de84f28d81d3ee56fe7bfe> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e4541027b9464b2f2eb8e01db938636c .
_:e4541027b9464b2f2eb8e01db938636c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5574a11134d33d66e3de84f28d81d3ee56fe7bfe> <http://schema.org/description> "Benthic monitoring of the sea bed adjacent to the fish farm as a requirement of the CAR licence for the site. Grab samples collected in proximity to the farm and at two reference locations. Samples analysed for: benthos, redox, psa, carbon." .
_:a891326c64a5972f58fb6fa7cfa519dd <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:557232db96e5dca0057cbd6c93d9ab29f26f1119> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ff1865926fd0dc53fe11e603d1b7c426 .
_:ff1865926fd0dc53fe11e603d1b7c426 <http://schema.org/value> "Fisheries Mapping Project" .
_:ff1865926fd0dc53fe11e603d1b7c426 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:557232db96e5dca0057cbd6c93d9ab29f26f1119> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a891326c64a5972f58fb6fa7cfa519dd .
_:a891326c64a5972f58fb6fa7cfa519dd <http://schema.org/value> "Eastern Sea Fisheries Joint Committee" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:557232db96e5dca0057cbd6c93d9ab29f26f1119> <http://schema.org/description> "This layer is the output of the Eastern Sea Fisheries Joint Committee's Fisheries Mapping Project, which aimed to describe-using best available data and fishermens knowledge-the extent of the main fisheries within the ESFJC District.\r\n \r\n They are not, however, exhaustive-please use with discretion. Use of this data should never replace full, proper consultation within the fishing industry, but rather be seen as illustrative of the types of activity within the District and, where information is available, an indication of seasonality. \r\n \r\n A report on the Fisheries Mapping Project will be available in Spring 2012, and will contain information about how the data was collected and compiled, and the process of consultation which was undertaken. Please refer to the ESFJC website: www.eastern-ifca.gov.uk\r\n \r\n For further details on the project, its output, or guidance on how to interpret the data, please contact the project manager: jwoo@esfjc.co.uk.\r\n \r\n To register for updates to these layers (including forthcoming addition of metadata), please register your interest at jwoo@esfjc.co.uk. \r\n \r\n (Please acknowledge use of Fisheries Mapping Project data. It can be cited as: ESFJC, 2010- ESFJC District Fisheries Mapping Project)." .
_:ff1865926fd0dc53fe11e603d1b7c426 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:a891326c64a5972f58fb6fa7cfa519dd <http://schema.org/value> "ESFJC" .
_:a891326c64a5972f58fb6fa7cfa519dd <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:557232db96e5dca0057cbd6c93d9ab29f26f1119> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:556ca1f9c7f8592539f88490521998289b0cbc3f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:cbe93710eafd8b9053084449cb634fca <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:cbe93710eafd8b9053084449cb634fca <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:556ca1f9c7f8592539f88490521998289b0cbc3f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:cbe93710eafd8b9053084449cb634fca .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:556ca1f9c7f8592539f88490521998289b0cbc3f> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by English Heritage to draw up and implement a Protocol for the reporting of sites and artefacts of historic environment interest discovered by the fishing industry during the course of their normal day-to-day activities. The Fishing Industry Protocol for Archaeological Discoveries (FIPAD) comprises a set a simple actions to be undertaken by the Finder, the FIPAD contact and the Archaeologist so that archaeological data can be accessioned to the national heritage record. The Protocol was trialled as a one year pilot project within the Sussex Inshore Fisheries and Conservation Authority (IFCA) District, starting April 2012." .
_:cbe93710eafd8b9053084449cb634fca <http://schema.org/value> "English Heritage" .
_:cbe93710eafd8b9053084449cb634fca <http://schema.org/value> "Wessex Archaeology" .
_:d22737723ce1d2821c2d143cc9ac7149 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:ae47ce71fc5fa2e72214ca92d3fb9e04 <http://schema.org/value> "Liverpool Bay" .
