_:a2a0dc4921d9ffe3de338f6728e1522a <http://schema.org/value> "Ormonde offshore wind farm" .
_:a2a0dc4921d9ffe3de338f6728e1522a <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5127069a17205151405f82c3d94eaa8ba07af8a7> <http://schema.org/description> "RPS contracted Wildfowl &amp; Wetlands Trust (Consulting) Limited (WWT Consulting) to provide weekly counts of peak numbers of Pink-footed Geese Anser brachyrhynchus and Whooper Swans Cygnus cygnus on the WWT Martin Mere reserve in Lancashire. These data were collected to inform consent licensing requirements at the Ormonde offshore wind farm, with the objective of determining whether the patterns of arrival of migrating Pink-footed Geese and Whooper Swans are impacted by the location of the offshore wind farms in the East Irish Sea. Counts were to take place from the week commencing 7th September to the week commencing 21st December, 2014." .
_:bcec8034e1477b2af267bb595e28ac0 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:d0dfee8e06af4a52d72fc5a5c0454242 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d0dfee8e06af4a52d72fc5a5c0454242 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5123f55f7ca36ca36f389e3701382296d36bc3af> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d0dfee8e06af4a52d72fc5a5c0454242 <http://schema.org/value> "Stakmap/Fishermap" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5123f55f7ca36ca36f389e3701382296d36bc3af> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d0dfee8e06af4a52d72fc5a5c0454242 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:5123f55f7ca36ca36f389e3701382296d36bc3af> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class records the number of wildlife enthusiasts carried on charter boats, it also records the number of vessels involved in this activity. Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
_:af281693cb7e2f04062175351105a5e3 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:512355cf1ef4a8a1d10401e3faf03bced28721ae> <http://schema.org/description> "Samples and associated geological data are held at the British Geological Survey for Maritime Coastguard Agency (MCA), Civil Hydrography Programme (CHP), Bathymetric Survey HI1240; Runabay Head to The Tuns (JIBS), Area in SqKm: 663, (31/12/2007 to 22/06/2008), Standard: IHO S44ed4 Order 1. Contract: INTERREG. FY 2008/09. Contractor: OSAE." .
_:a571a85660884a7c81d8084533e17f63 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
