<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:50d0e4c38c9da51ba40663b64805a99b392028a0> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e778f49bd0f60b30fbef6e661fff9c76 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:50d0e4c38c9da51ba40663b64805a99b392028a0> <http://schema.org/description> "This collection comprises 85 site images from an intermittent archaeological watching brief at Kinterbury Point undertaken by Cotswold Archaeology from January 2019 to September 2020. Also known as Bull Point, the site is an ordnance store constructed between 1851 and 1854. The watching brief recorded a series of modern made ground deposits, tramways, a World War II-era bomb shelter and concrete floor slabs associated with demolished 20th-century buildings." .
_:e778f49bd0f60b30fbef6e661fff9c76 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
