_:a862c830f02333c3ef583954819ad7af <http://schema.org/value> "Essex" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4e613d76217087d8b56d619bbb1a2160e5d8c480> <http://schema.org/description> "Record of Tenellia adspersa from St. Osyth in Essex. In the course of a survey of the fauna of the Borrow Dykes of north east Essex, carried out by Wilson and Wilson, a visit was made to Howlands marsh, an Essex Wildlife Trust Reserve, near St. Osyth on July 23rd 1998. This survey was collated by MarLIN as part of a data collation contract for species on the provisional list of nationally important marine features (Lieberknecht et al. 2004)." .
_:aa3761e4f96776bff3853b18c16d5d5e <http://schema.org/name> "taxon" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4e430d226de5b0c63ef15ef39e354838dd4e4257> <http://schema.org/description> "WESTLINE was acquired by BIRPS (the British Institutions Reflection Profiling Syndicate). The seismic data image the faulted conjugate margins of the Rockall Trough and the intrabasinal sediments. The seismic data were shot to 18 s two-way time along a single 450 km-long transect." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4e430d226de5b0c63ef15ef39e354838dd4e4257> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fc74f9a98e8dea85802acd780f409311 .
