_:b8c9f51232da98558582745d1a78a36c <http://schema.org/value> "sea bed levels" .
_:b8c9f51232da98558582745d1a78a36c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ef71e29fe076fd1347b50d32c37e7ef9 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4b94e76a548da3dfe7c6e67904afbb41ad1365cc> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b8c9f51232da98558582745d1a78a36c .
_:ef71e29fe076fd1347b50d32c37e7ef9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b8c9f51232da98558582745d1a78a36c <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:c89b3a74ae751feb988187edca13871f <http://schema.org/value> "Race Bank" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4b94e76a548da3dfe7c6e67904afbb41ad1365cc> <http://schema.org/description> "Centrica Renewable Energy Limited (CREL) has commissioned ABP Marine Environmental Research Ltd (ABPmer) to investigate future morphological change across the Race Bank offshore wind farm site, with a view to providing estimations of future bed levels change at individual turbine locations. In particular, the work has developed estimations of the potential deepest and shallowest sea bed levels that are likely to be encountered over the next 20 and 40 years." .
_:c89b3a74ae751feb988187edca13871f <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4b94e76a548da3dfe7c6e67904afbb41ad1365cc> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ef71e29fe076fd1347b50d32c37e7ef9 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4b85163ceddd6b1f303da368c225324e20755d49> <http://schema.org/description> "This project details trawl surveys and benthic grab surveys that were carried out by CMACS at London Array Offshore Wind Farm site.\r\n\r\nTrawl surveys were completed during the following periods: April 21-27 2003, July 7-15 2003, December 6-11 2003 and February 20-26 2004. On each occasion trawls were carried out at forty three locations around the study area and seventeen locations along the cable route options.\r\n\r\nA comprehensive grab sampling survey, refined after consultation with English Nature, CEFAS and the Kent and Essex Sea Fisheries Committee, was carried out during the summer of 2004. Coverage was not spread evenly over the study area, but was more concentrated where a variety of seabed types were expected within a small area and more widely spread where the seabed was expected to be more uniform over a broad area. This method was adopted with teh ais of British Geological Survey maps and Admiralty Charts." .
_:a4e96491fbd5eb388f2bc33b37e94d1 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
_:bc7a2f9f698087a6a743ebedefda5f86 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:b4540ca2d634c0725c998fd26c991a5 <http://schema.org/value> "Kent and Essex Sea Fisheries Committee" .
_:a4e96491fbd5eb388f2bc33b37e94d1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
