<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:433bb9a02fda473f2ec8c83d86b1691d16a00ae7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:c54c677ac6f8774e559b3c0764de1032 <http://schema.org/value> "Lidar - bathymetric survey" .
_:c54c677ac6f8774e559b3c0764de1032 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c54c677ac6f8774e559b3c0764de1032 <http://schema.org/name> "procedures" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:433bb9a02fda473f2ec8c83d86b1691d16a00ae7> <http://schema.org/description> "This processed bathymetric data set has been derived from a Lidar - bathymetric survey. The source data was collected, validated and processed for the purpose of Safety Of Life At Sea (SOLAS). The data set must not be used for navigation or to create products that could be used for navigation." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:433bb9a02fda473f2ec8c83d86b1691d16a00ae7> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:c54c677ac6f8774e559b3c0764de1032 .
_:a1c1f457ae18be01a48ee46897425ada <http://schema.org/value> "Southern North Sea" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:4334b7bc6b4fb0ace16b15d7cb77066a44b2385d> <http://schema.org/description> "Using regulator guidance, this Navigational Risk Assessment (NRA) identifies and analyses both the base case and future case risk associated with the development of Dogger Bank Teesside A &amp; B. Analysis and collision risk modelling was undertaken based on three scenarios as follows: Dogger Bank Teesside A in isolation, Dogger Bank Teesside B in isolation and Dogger Bank Teesside A &amp; B together.\r\n\r\nThe NRA includes an assessment of existing navigational features including metocean data, maritime incidents and a marine traffic survey (AIS and Radar) to identify the baseline environment. The elements of the Rochdale Envelope have then been assessed against the base case to identify areas or activities that may see a change in risk following development of Dogger Bank Teesside A &amp; B.\r\n\r\nConsultation was undertaken with stakeholders, regular operators identified from the marine traffic survey and European Shipping Associations. In order to address the cumulative issue in the Southern North Sea, Forewind joined Hornsea and East Anglia developers in forming the Southern North Sea Offshore Wind Forum (SNSOWF) and further consultations were undertaken as part of this work.\r\n\r\nThe marine traffic survey identified seven main routes operating within a 10 nautical mile (nm) buffer around Dogger Bank Teesside A &amp; B with the majority of vessel types transiting on these routes being tankers and cargo vessels. Fishing activity was recorded across much of the sites with a high density of vessels to the north of Dogger Bank Teesside B. The level of recreational vessel activity was noted as being very low." .
_:bc9abaa4cf27e2056b51a58f55022b16 <http://schema.org/value> "Forewind" .
_:bc9abaa4cf27e2056b51a58f55022b16 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:a1c1f457ae18be01a48ee46897425ada <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
