<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:42fa8842c6bde7310654b4716f10ac9091b656fd> <http://schema.org/description> "Sabellaria spinulosa presence records from detailed video and photo tow sledge surveys in Dorset, 20 miles south of Anvil Point. The study of the bottom fauna and bedforms in this tide-swept region of the English Channel was conducted using a towed sledge fitted with photographic and TV cameras. This added to previous data collected by side-scan sonar. Data was collated by MarLIN for the provisional list of Nationally Important Marine Features." .
