_:a752b67dcd14deb20b916f556a86d698 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:a3df6b54d81c247e0e0f7a8ab5c15166 <http://schema.org/value> "time series measurements" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d9a61019e3b7125735f3af0e97d2e707aeed683> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a752b67dcd14deb20b916f556a86d698 .
_:e294e0043df0a4b6dec1a21721f9a7de <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d92c2c8d40805669e02f9d7b06421f619c863e8> <http://schema.org/description> "An oil and gas industry site survey for seabed infrastructure (anchoring conditions) acquired in March 2006. The block number traversed was 21/30." .
_:e294e0043df0a4b6dec1a21721f9a7de <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e294e0043df0a4b6dec1a21721f9a7de <http://schema.org/value> "block number traversed" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d92c2c8d40805669e02f9d7b06421f619c863e8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d92c2c8d40805669e02f9d7b06421f619c863e8> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e294e0043df0a4b6dec1a21721f9a7de .
_:af30d95997aa168641e8c7edda89cf8e <http://schema.org/value> "Suffolk coast" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d9298bcab8708968db538bc642cc45332aab9f5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d9298bcab8708968db538bc642cc45332aab9f5> <http://schema.org/description> "Greater Gabbard Offshore Winds Ltd have recently completed the construction of a wind farm approximately\r\n14mi east of Suffolk coast.\r\nThe offshore wind farm consists of 152 Wind Turbine Generators (WTGs) with a gross nameplate capacity of\r\napproximately 504MW. The project is now fully operational and the construction was completed in September\r\n2012.\r\nOne element of the windfarm that preceded its development and has continued through the construction phase into operations is the construction of two metrological masts (IGMMZ and IGMMX). This series includes IGMMZ which was constructed in 2005 and has recorded various elements at 10 minute intervals and sent the readings back to shore via a SCADA communications system." .
_:af30d95997aa168641e8c7edda89cf8e <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:af30d95997aa168641e8c7edda89cf8e <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d9298bcab8708968db538bc642cc45332aab9f5> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:af30d95997aa168641e8c7edda89cf8e .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d800579c931ff2f3120dde1885a334a85396bbb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:a8e333c43d7c0b1b1470cdff78401dbb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f1e8ab5e5bff7d7f6303bdc46b922e00 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:dcaea6b95c404144b55e4b0c8ba90ec0 <http://schema.org/value> "Brough Head Wave Farm Limited" .
_:f1e8ab5e5bff7d7f6303bdc46b922e00 <http://schema.org/value> "point of Howana Geo" .
_:dcaea6b95c404144b55e4b0c8ba90ec0 <http://schema.org/value> "Aquamarine Power Limited" .
_:dcaea6b95c404144b55e4b0c8ba90ec0 <http://schema.org/value> "SSE Renewables UK Limited" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d800579c931ff2f3120dde1885a334a85396bbb> <http://schema.org/description> "Optimised Environments Ltd (OPEN) has been appointed to undertake the Seascape, Landscape and Visual\r\nImpact Assessment (SLVIA) as part of the EIA for the Outshore Point Wave Farm. The Brough Head Wave Farm\r\nproject, proposed by Brough Head Wave Farm Limited (BHWFL) is a partnership between renewable technology\r\ndeveloper Aquamarine Power Limited (Aquamarine Power) and SSE Renewables UK Limited (SSER). The aim is\r\nto develop the first 50 MW of the Brough Head Wave Farm at Outshore Point (herein refered to as ‘the Project’).\r\nThe Project is located off Mainland Orkney, in the vicinity of Outshore Point between the point of Howana Geo\r\nand Marwick Bay." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3d800579c931ff2f3120dde1885a334a85396bbb> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a8e333c43d7c0b1b1470cdff78401dbb .
