_:af188cd542c43377888e4cbea9c0f746 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Scotland" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3beb5202e952f2da482307afde5973f3e654b0b9> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fc9306110644d7773d7672fb72809767 .
_:fc9306110644d7773d7672fb72809767 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3beb5202e952f2da482307afde5973f3e654b0b9> <http://schema.org/description> "EMU Limited was commissioned by Lincs Wind Farm Limited to undertake an urgent survey for unexploded\r\nordnance (UXO) at positions KP 2.0 to 15.0 of the two proposed Lincs export cable routes located in The Wash\r\nregion. The survey comprised the collection of swath bathymetry, magnetometer and sidescan sonar data.\r\nThe survey was carried out on a 12 hour operational basis using the vessel EMU Surveyor between the 17th\r\nJune and 28th June 2011. In order to achieve project objectives a GeoSwath interferometric multibeam system\r\nand 3 Geometrics G-882 magnetometers were used. Tidal data were acquired for bathymetry reduction\r\nthrough the collection of GPS height data on board the survey vessel. Nene Surveyor was used to survey\r\nbetween KP 2.0 to 1.1 between the 28th June and 1st July 2011 because EMU Surveyor was unable to work in\r\nthese shallow waters. Additional survey work was carried out between 28th July and 30th July 2011 on Nab Cat\r\nII between KP 2.0 to 1.1" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3beb5202e952f2da482307afde5973f3e654b0b9> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d77f6f119caef3fc26555e32913486cc .
