<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:36847f7bbf0b653f7207eaf0304d3a1b958974a1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:af300d48022c39c656bb0be8cc2dd4f2 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:36847f7bbf0b653f7207eaf0304d3a1b958974a1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:da671f1423273c91fa429ffc51cf17ec .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:36847f7bbf0b653f7207eaf0304d3a1b958974a1> <http://schema.org/description> "The Port of London Authority (PLA) Hydrographic Service was commissioned by DONG\r\nEnergy to undertake a Multibeam Echosounder (MBES) survey at the Gunfleet Sands 3\r\nOffshore Windfarm in the Thames Estuary.\r\nThe scope of work, for the April/May 2014 survey included:\r\n\r\n1. MBES survey of 50m wide corridor along Export Cable Route between the\r\nWTG F0 and the HDD exit point [See Figure 1].\r\n2. MBES survey of the WTG foundations F00 and G)) and inter-array cable.\r\n\r\nThis series covers survey elements which were undertaken on the 10th April and 16th May\r\n2014, along the Export Cable Route and around Turbines F00 and G00. The survey work\r\nwas carried out using the PLA survey vessel ‘Yantlet’, with bathymetric data being collected\r\nusing a hull-mounted Reson SeaBat 8125h MBES." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:36847f7bbf0b653f7207eaf0304d3a1b958974a1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:c5600f65a2e6ecaf4be7bb146cf02db6 <http://schema.org/name> "migratory marine species" .
