<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:351e4427b6c27c83b30d8fbdb7dd7343f4ad343d> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:abc2caad0f18f82ef189500ce48cd9a8 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:351e4427b6c27c83b30d8fbdb7dd7343f4ad343d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:abc2caad0f18f82ef189500ce48cd9a8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:abc2caad0f18f82ef189500ce48cd9a8 <http://schema.org/value> "MCT" .
_:abc2caad0f18f82ef189500ce48cd9a8 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:351e4427b6c27c83b30d8fbdb7dd7343f4ad343d> <http://schema.org/description> "In terms of suitability for deployment of their tidal generation devices MCT has requested development of the high resolution Coastal Science Kyle Rhea hydrodynamic model, including small scale variations within the area of interest, by incorporating high resolution multi-beam bathymetry and ADCP time series data.\r\nIt is considered that the present status of the model is such that it represents a suitable tool for further hydrodynamic characterisation of the area of interest at this stage, and as dictated by project requirements. Further calibration and validation will give added confidence to the model predictions." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:351968d4ed25199c637c930df13209a46c715358> <http://schema.org/description> "GeoSurv conducted an data re-interpretation of the EMU (2208) and Osiris (2013) geophysical data in relation to the micrositing of the turbines within the defined Turbine Box Area. The purpose of the investigations was to ascertain any major geohazards that could be observed from the combined bathymetry, side scan sonar and sub-bottom profiler datasets.\r\n\r\nThe focus of the study is to look at the water depth, distribution of sediments and where possible the thickness of surficial cover at the four primary and four secondary turbine locations" .
_:e00943e3aa3a67860ba3d3696bce0759 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
