_:aa491e3f59e2d064732471559a5e3f3d <http://schema.org/value> "Anatec" .
_:aa491e3f59e2d064732471559a5e3f3d <http://schema.org/value> "AIS" .
_:aa491e3f59e2d064732471559a5e3f3d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34360acf7708af68c748f9e58e1f6de2b1caff23> <http://schema.org/description> "Anatec were commissioned by Centrica Renewable Energy Ltd to assess the risk of damage to their planned cable route in The Wash from vessels dragging anchor and from emergency anchoring. This report presents an update to the risk assessment, using 12 months of AIS data collected from September 2011 to August 2012.\r\nThis report summarises the data sources, methodology and results. The results are presented in terms of the annual frequency of an anchor dragging over the cable or a vessel dropping anchor on the cable; and the frequency of cable damage, based on the as-laid burial depth of the cable and the estimated anchor penetration depth." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34360acf7708af68c748f9e58e1f6de2b1caff23> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34360acf7708af68c748f9e58e1f6de2b1caff23> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:aa491e3f59e2d064732471559a5e3f3d .
_:d69ffcd47801cbeba1f39a38a7316d7d <http://schema.org/value> "Eastern Sea Fisheries Joint Committee" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34214bd242e149d14bcef3797bb8874c03893f6f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b7189eae1676ec384dedb7e46722aeac .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34214bd242e149d14bcef3797bb8874c03893f6f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d69ffcd47801cbeba1f39a38a7316d7d .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:34214bd242e149d14bcef3797bb8874c03893f6f> <http://schema.org/description> "This layer is the output of the Eastern Sea Fisheries Joint Committee's Fisheries Mapping Project, which aimed to describe-using best available data and fishermens knowledge-the extent of the main fisheries within the ESFJC District.\r\n \r\n They are not, however, exhaustive-please use with discretion. Use of this data should never replace full, proper consultation within the fishing industry, but rather be seen as illustrative of the types of activity within the District and, where information is available, an indication of seasonality. \r\n A report on the Fisheries Mapping Project will be available in Spring 2012, and will contain information about how the data was collected and compiled, and the process of consultation which was undertaken. Please refer to the ESFJC website: www.eastern-ifca.gov.uk\r\n \r\n For further details on the project, its output, or guidance on how to interpret the data, please contact the project manager: jwoo@esfjc.co.uk.\r\n \r\n To register for updates to these layers (including forthcoming addition of metadata), please register your interest at jwoo@esfjc.co.uk. \r\n \r\n (Please acknowledge use of Fisheries Mapping Project data. It can be cited as: ESFJC, 2010- ESFJC District Fisheries Mapping Project)." .
_:d69ffcd47801cbeba1f39a38a7316d7d <http://schema.org/value> "ESFJC" .
