_:bf5eab55780443eb8eb2e3dcc519dbc8 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:341616dae6b137e0f6957ab43a08fe50bd1e5979> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b72c5ba684c45e27d48118c78d8ebbe8 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:341616dae6b137e0f6957ab43a08fe50bd1e5979> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:bf5eab55780443eb8eb2e3dcc519dbc8 <http://schema.org/value> "National Oceanography Centre" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:341616dae6b137e0f6957ab43a08fe50bd1e5979> <http://schema.org/description> "This joint British Geological Survey (BGS) and National Oceanography Centre, Southampton (NOCS) marine multibeam and geophysical survey took place in September 2010 in Lake Windermere on board the RV White Ribbon. The purpose was to produce a bathymetric map of the lake, in a bid to determine the late glacial and post glacial processes, using sediments from within Windermere and identification of lakebed habitats. Sea floor bathymetry data were collected using a Kongsberg EM3002D multibeam system. These data are archived by BGS." .
_:bf5eab55780443eb8eb2e3dcc519dbc8 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:b72c5ba684c45e27d48118c78d8ebbe8 <http://schema.org/value> "Lake Windermere" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:340f83b18d952eccb9b9cc9280d4ab65a5624fb3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:db7b513de84d6af99c2e80619b51f385 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:db7b513de84d6af99c2e80619b51f385 <http://schema.org/value> "GEO" .
_:db7b513de84d6af99c2e80619b51f385 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:340f83b18d952eccb9b9cc9280d4ab65a5624fb3> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:db7b513de84d6af99c2e80619b51f385 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:340f83b18d952eccb9b9cc9280d4ab65a5624fb3> <http://schema.org/description> "Scira Offshore Energy Ltd. contracted GEO to deliver equipment and personnel for a geotechnical\r\nsite investigation for offshore windmill foundations and substations. The works were performed from the Company supplied vessel “Geofjord” between 29th September and 16th October 2008. The investigation included 101 continuous CPTs (CPTU) in 86 locations with GEO’s 20 tons seabed rig ”SCOPE”.\r\nThis Report 1 Part B describes the Geotechnical Data acquisition from the field operation\r\naccording to NORSOK Standard G-001. Report 1 Part C describes the Field Operations conducted during the offshore operations." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:33f6782e7bb78826a5e20c7242d30bd4267e1582> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b59e3eb3a820c94495aeffcded917497 .
_:b59e3eb3a820c94495aeffcded917497 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:b59e3eb3a820c94495aeffcded917497 <http://schema.org/value> "Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Limited" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:33f6782e7bb78826a5e20c7242d30bd4267e1582> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:d0118d6c7b9e22f8e9402355b9b69b2 .
_:d0118d6c7b9e22f8e9402355b9b69b2 <http://schema.org/value> "Blyth Offshore Demonstration Project" .
_:b59e3eb3a820c94495aeffcded917497 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:d0118d6c7b9e22f8e9402355b9b69b2 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:d0118d6c7b9e22f8e9402355b9b69b2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:33f6782e7bb78826a5e20c7242d30bd4267e1582> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:33f6782e7bb78826a5e20c7242d30bd4267e1582> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology has been commissioned by Blyth Offshore Demonstrator Limited (BODL) to\r\nundertake an archaeological assessment of the Unexploded Ordnance (UXO) Clearance and\r\nDisposal survey data attained for the Export Cable Route (ECR) and the Wind Turbine Array 2,\r\nundertaken in 2016 as part of the Blyth Offshore Demonstration Project. This document has been\r\nprepared to detail the results of that assessment.\r\nThe archaeological assessment began with a review of the Target Investigation Reports prepared\r\nby the contractor commissioned to carry out the inspection and clearance (N-Sea). These included\r\n‘as found’ co-ordinates for the targets, a brief description of the material, and video stills and sonar\r\ndata. The assessment categorised targets based on archaeological interest, archaeological value\r\nand confidence of assessment. Where it was determined that further information was required to\r\ninform the archaeological assessment, the Remotely Operated Vehicle (ROV) video was requested\r\nfor further assessment." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:33ee3d390b9fb5e0faf1fa740bc05a8eabc0d678> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
