<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3381acd5b29935bd0a9bc7f51b411f1332406421> <http://schema.org/description> "This project sought to provide a desk-based review of cable installation techniques and protection used for offshore wind and other cables related projects in order to better understand how seabed habitats are affected by such activity. The project collated and assessed information on cable installation techniques used in the UK, and considered the effectiveness of these installation methods and tools in different seabed types. The project also collated and assessed information on the impacts of cabling on seabed habitats and communities, and provided a series of recommendations for future consent applications and proposals for best working practices during and after cable installation." .
_:f2c10a8e584449406a0f90401928b9e1 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3381acd5b29935bd0a9bc7f51b411f1332406421> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:f2c10a8e584449406a0f90401928b9e1 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:f2c10a8e584449406a0f90401928b9e1 <http://schema.org/value> "UK" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3381acd5b29935bd0a9bc7f51b411f1332406421> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f2c10a8e584449406a0f90401928b9e1 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:337f8ed64cee91e970f22beb76037bedaa9b141a> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bd4e0b53ee382244512dd77263a3e5e1 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:337f8ed64cee91e970f22beb76037bedaa9b141a> <http://schema.org/description> "This series includes the reporting and data deliverables for seasonal aerial surveys of seabirds and marine mammals east of Shetland in the Scottish Northern Isles. The surveys were completed as part of POSEIDON, a multi-year, multi-partner project funded through The Crown Estate OWEC programme and led by Natural England. The series constitutes: \r\n\r\nThe first seasonal (September to October 2023) report outlining results from digital aerial surveys conducted in September 2023 within the Northern Isles under the POSEIDON project and commissioned by Natural England. Surveys were undertaken using APEM’s high-resolution camera system to capture digital still imagery of birds and marine megafauna within the Survey Area. The survey was successfully carried out across one day in September 2023. A total of 4,851 observations were recorded during the survey in September 2023, of which 4,769 were observations \r\nof birds and 82 were observations of marine megafauna" .
_:d2be0a980cdf40db350a96603afae1e2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
