_:a4afdceec401dbf9ad9af9802d5adfe5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:302e170447da61692fd6ce363ae0e5a621e9b6fb> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 45 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, from across the Barents Sea and Norwegian Sea areas specifically at the following sections: Svinoey NW, Gimsoey NW, Fugloeya-Bjoernoeya, Vardoe N. Data were collected during January 2001. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the Institute of Marine Research, Norway as part of the Monitoring the Atlantic Inflow toward the Arctic (MAIA) project." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:3029d554e579d27f13d12f7324ff178b2b099d6d> <http://schema.org/description> "Fugro EMU Limited (Fugro EMU) was commissioned by Scira Offshore Energy Limited to conduct a\r\nbathymetry and sidescan sonar survey of the Sheringham Shoal Offshore Wind Farm, a prescribed\r\ntransit route and cable export corridor. The survey was required to fulfil Marine Management\r\nOrganisation (MMO) requirements for post-construction monitoring of scour, trenched cables and\r\ndebris.\r\nIn order to meet these requirements, the scope of work required that Fugro EMU provide the following\r\ndeliverables and reports:\r\n? Accurate bathymetry across the Wind Farm and along the export corridors\r\n? High resolution sidescan sonar across the entire survey area\r\n? An archaeological assessment by subcontractor, Wessex Archaeology\r\nThe survey was undertaken between 1st November 2013 and 3rd December 2013 on board RV\r\nDiscovery, all survey objectives and contractual requirements were achieved." .
_:cf1e3824ab1954577bb9c63e7019a4cc <http://schema.org/value> "Scira Offshore Energy Limited" .
_:cf1e3824ab1954577bb9c63e7019a4cc <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
