_:e395e1993956c039079cd8cb415b5b7d <http://schema.org/value> "Continental Shelf Unit II" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2e45fdaeee19f2e9daa180fd78a868b6f896ab6a> <http://schema.org/description> "This sampling survey has been carried out by Continental Shelf Unit II of British Geological Survey (BGS) for BGS, the survey took place from June to July 1971 off the west coast of Scotland and Minch on board the MV Surveyor. The purpose was to collect data as part of a regional mapping programme. Sample data were collected using vibrocorer, gravity corer (rock and sediment), shipek grab and beach sampling. These data are archived by BGS. No BGS survey report currently available, IGS 1971 annual report contains summary." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2e45fdaeee19f2e9daa180fd78a868b6f896ab6a> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e2a3fa1181801f2d9df4771b288aff25 .
