_:d88a71df52e4edbcbfceb854a8d96acb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2de8e4d7abe6954b3aefe610743070646add2878> <http://schema.org/description> "This processed bathymetric data set has been derived from a Lidar - topographic survey. The source data was collected, validated and processed for the purpose of Safety Of Life At Sea (SOLAS). The data set must not be used for navigation or to create products that could be used for navigation." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2de8e4d7abe6954b3aefe610743070646add2878> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:d88a71df52e4edbcbfceb854a8d96acb <http://schema.org/value> "Lidar - topographic survey" .
_:bc671d304623717906855ab8e7b296fa <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2dd0d6ef56233ad826136b48bbc4a2d29e17d6c2> <http://schema.org/description> "Wessex Archaeology was commissioned by Centrica Renewable Energy Ltd. to undertake Stage 2 geoarchaeological recording on borehole samples recovered from the proposed Race Bank Offshore Wind Farm site. This Stage 2 recording follows on from recommendations made in the Stage 1 assessment report, and focuses on the potential for the preservation of archaeological and\r\npalaeoenvironmental material in the samples selected during the Stage 1 assessment.\r\nOf the previously established stratigraphic sequence, it was found that sediments from Units\r\n1c and 1d (terrestrial peat, organic clay and silt) contain potentially well-preserved organic\r\nmaterial suitable for palaeoenvironmental analysis, and that an eroded and re-deposited section of Unit 2 could also contain similar material.\r\nThis report makes proposals for the Stage 3 geoarchaeological sub-sampling and assessment of 19 samples (51 sub-samples) taken from nine of the recorded samples from six cores, as Units 1c and 1d are deemed to be of possible archaeological and\r\npalaeoenvironmental importance." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2dd0d6ef56233ad826136b48bbc4a2d29e17d6c2> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bc671d304623717906855ab8e7b296fa .
_:bc671d304623717906855ab8e7b296fa <http://schema.org/value> "Wessex Archaeology" .
_:bc671d304623717906855ab8e7b296fa <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:bc671d304623717906855ab8e7b296fa <http://schema.org/value> "Centrica Renewable Energy Ltd." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2dd0d6ef56233ad826136b48bbc4a2d29e17d6c2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:e158631016af90ea97ceb0000d6312f0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2dcdf21f9f25e3dbb139767d12192fcea23a8c6c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e79090ef53c424d3724f6f16e6889d1a .
_:e158631016af90ea97ceb0000d6312f0 <http://schema.org/value> "MS47 sidescan sonar" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2dcdf21f9f25e3dbb139767d12192fcea23a8c6c> <http://schema.org/description> "This British Geological Survey (BGS) regional marine sampling survey took place in April 1978 in Northern North Sea and around Shetland Islands on board the RRS John Murray. These purpose was to collect data as part of a continuation of geochemical sampling programme of superficial bottom seiment for heavy metal analysis. Sea floor data was attempted using MS47 sidescan sonar, equipment failed, no records available.Seabed samples and cores were collected using Shipek grab and a Reineck box corer. These data are archived by BGS. Details of the survey are contained in BGS cruise summary." .
_:e79090ef53c424d3724f6f16e6889d1a <http://schema.org/value> "BGS" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2dcdf21f9f25e3dbb139767d12192fcea23a8c6c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f7062404a38f950ad54ca4f93bf65031 .
_:e158631016af90ea97ceb0000d6312f0 <http://schema.org/value> "Shipek grab" .
_:e79090ef53c424d3724f6f16e6889d1a <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
