_:e1812ff85dd42a8cb444e0acdf64c363 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2d1033c0ab1987ca8e3e22874682ebe1b6a09d1b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:e1812ff85dd42a8cb444e0acdf64c363 <http://schema.org/value> "Deal" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2d1033c0ab1987ca8e3e22874682ebe1b6a09d1b> <http://schema.org/description> "During the summer of 2017 a maritime archaeological excavation on a 17th century shipwreck was carried out on the Goodwin Sands off the coast of Deal in Kent, England. The project was both initiated and funded by the Dutch state's Cultural Heritage Agency, as the shipwreck was known to be that of the Dutch East Indiaman called the 'Rooswijk'. The protected wreck is currently on Historic England's Heritage at Risk Register (HAR), and faces declining conditions with major localised problems. Over 1800 objects were found, including part of the cargo, equipment and possible personal artefacts. Amongst the equipment were three copper alloy objects: a cauldron, a pan and a lid." .
_:e1812ff85dd42a8cb444e0acdf64c363 <http://schema.org/value> "England" .
_:e1812ff85dd42a8cb444e0acdf64c363 <http://schema.org/value> "Goodwin Sands" .
_:b6789a33123f6f7ea4c627392a5b2d46 <http://schema.org/value> "Dutch state's Cultural Heritage Agency" .
_:e1812ff85dd42a8cb444e0acdf64c363 <http://schema.org/value> "Kent" .
_:a97a098f21da16051a45502c88afbbeb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
