_:ffa3c05e0b5ba0af32c5e9fc94c0886 <http://schema.org/value> "Agulhas Current region" .
_:d2b19708940834cc82419ff71d6ae5fa <http://schema.org/value> "James Rennell Centre for Ocean Circulation" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2c36a7f586f9b6def49b0a9d94450e17375172a6> <http://schema.org/description> "The dataset comprises 15 hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during February - March 1995. The cruise, part of the World Ocean Circulation Experiment (WOCE) Indian Special Survey (ISS01), worked stations in the Agulhas Current region of the Southern Indian Ocean, 30 - 33 S, 29 - 34 E. A complete list of all data parameters are described by the SeaDataNet Parameter Discovery Vocabulary (PDV) keywords assigned in this metadata record. The data were collected by the James Rennell Centre for Ocean Circulation as part of the World Ocean Circulation Experiment (WOCE)." .
_:da941909dbe4f0f597ff7af6f6410fa8 <http://schema.org/value> "hydrographic data profiles" .
_:da941909dbe4f0f597ff7af6f6410fa8 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2c36a7f586f9b6def49b0a9d94450e17375172a6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2c36a7f586f9b6def49b0a9d94450e17375172a6> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ffa3c05e0b5ba0af32c5e9fc94c0886 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2c2fa0e383994226dd8597214e43d75df3c4c306> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a6b570e266b3486b99a86b9ab22c160d .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2c2fa0e383994226dd8597214e43d75df3c4c306> <http://schema.org/description> "Subacoustech Environmental has undertaken a study to model the potential impact underwater noise generated by piling operations during the construction of the Triton Knoll Offshore Wind Farm (TKOWF) could have on local populations of fish (specifically, herring, sole and lemon sole) and marine mammals (specifically, harbour porpoise and harbour and grey seals). \r\nThe levels of underwater noise from the installation of 7.0 m and 8.5 m diameter piles at two representative piling locations have been estimated using a proprietary underwater sound propagation model (INSPIRE v18) that enables the level of noise from the piling and its behaviour with range to be estimated for varying tidal conditions, water depths and piling locations. The model is based on, and validated against, an existing database of measurements of piling noise." .
_:eca30a6e239e4120254f532fc4a14487 <http://schema.org/value> "sole" .
_:eca30a6e239e4120254f532fc4a14487 <http://schema.org/value> "herring" .
