_:e19c0311feb1b1ee2d0de613783c8ebd <http://schema.org/value> "Delft University of Technology" .
_:ffeed5ac0400a3d4bd0311df282c5564 <http://schema.org/value> "English waters" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2b9ae202db32fed6ee50232b2acbefb7ead9a771> <http://schema.org/description> "Author: EMU Ltd, Delft University of Technology and TG Marine.Report number: Report_08_P33. The aim of this study was to review the current marine aggregate dredging practices and technology as used in English waters and to examine best practices, movel equipment and technology in use worldwide. This project will indicate where opportunities for developing or improving practice may exist. Dredging practice, case studies and equipment from around the world were examined and they were assessed to see whether they are applicable, necessary or realistic for the English Industry." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2b8c4e1ca6a3900d422e0ee8e2e6f8b5db5dc2ea> <http://schema.org/description> "Phase 1 of the construction of an offshore wind farm situated midway between the Kent and Essex coastlines and more than 20km from each shore. Phase 1 comprises 175 turbines, 2 offshore substations, and 4 export cables to the shore. This particular part of the project is the archaeological assessment of marine geophysical survey data acquired during April 2014 and undertaken by the London Array Retained Archaeologist's as part of the three year programme of post-installation archaeological monitoring between 2013-2015." .
