_:a51be2881402797a9151afb49d901343 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:b0b4faea1de924c3819d3eda2fcc6a1b <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:a51be2881402797a9151afb49d901343 <http://schema.org/value> "Cone Penetration Tests" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaff2f8e2dd471f2b729f4df2f3a2ff92cd2851> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaff2f8e2dd471f2b729f4df2f3a2ff92cd2851> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b0b4faea1de924c3819d3eda2fcc6a1b .
_:b0b4faea1de924c3819d3eda2fcc6a1b <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaff2f8e2dd471f2b729f4df2f3a2ff92cd2851> <http://schema.org/description> "N-Sea Offshore BV have been awarded a contract by E.ON (Rampion Offshore Windfarm Ltd.) to provide geotechnical services as part of ground preparation works for the proposed Rampion Offshore Windfarm off the South coast of the UK. Marine Sampling Holland BV was contracted by N-Sea Offshore BV to perform the Cone Penetration Tests to supplement the risk assessment and review of vessel jack up locations. The operations started on the 16th of March 2016. This Series contains 2 reports, a set of appendices and the coordinate locations for the CPTs." .
_:b0b4faea1de924c3819d3eda2fcc6a1b <http://schema.org/value> "E.ON" .
_:b4a3499b99ddf66e7fcb98d459df38e2 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:bb0054ec77c3e29e6ae549e3232d3e46 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:bb0054ec77c3e29e6ae549e3232d3e46 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Biological Association" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaef1334f9bc3c093912c7d2f1896beecfa3ab1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bb0054ec77c3e29e6ae549e3232d3e46 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaef1334f9bc3c093912c7d2f1896beecfa3ab1> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b4a3499b99ddf66e7fcb98d459df38e2 .
_:b4a3499b99ddf66e7fcb98d459df38e2 <http://schema.org/value> "Crab Watch" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaef1334f9bc3c093912c7d2f1896beecfa3ab1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:bb0054ec77c3e29e6ae549e3232d3e46 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaef1334f9bc3c093912c7d2f1896beecfa3ab1> <http://schema.org/description> "Crab Watch was a European citizen science project run by the Marine Biological Association. It was a EU horizon 2020 funded project. Data was collated from mobile phone app for ad hoc sightings (developed by Coreo) and sightings input into the website." .
_:b4a3499b99ddf66e7fcb98d459df38e2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:ffc690a619cd2571c269acbb96addc45 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaea3c77370e0196684b0ae880bc838a5fce50c> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ffc690a619cd2571c269acbb96addc45 .
_:ffc690a619cd2571c269acbb96addc45 <http://schema.org/value> "Civil Hydrography Programme" .
_:ffc690a619cd2571c269acbb96addc45 <http://schema.org/value> "Maritime Coastguard Agency (MCA)" .
_:ffc690a619cd2571c269acbb96addc45 <http://schema.org/value> "MMT UK" .
_:ffc690a619cd2571c269acbb96addc45 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaea3c77370e0196684b0ae880bc838a5fce50c> <http://schema.org/description> "Samples and associated geological data are held at the British Geological Survey for Maritime Coastguard Agency (MCA), Civil Hydrography Programme (CHP), Bathymetric Survey HI1480; Western Approach to Off Casquets TSS, Area in SqKm: 1413, (01/05/2015 to 01/06/2015), Standard: IHO S44ed5 Order 1a. Contract: Medium. FY 2015/16. Contractor: MMT UK." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aaea3c77370e0196684b0ae880bc838a5fce50c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:ffc690a619cd2571c269acbb96addc45 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:be1645a288fecd982443cfb8fc762c1c <http://schema.org/value> "Northern Ireland" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aa7e9398426084ba7e40f134767d8cd6aa7eada> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:bed27070617b6aa64203d19390a33f4 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aa7e9398426084ba7e40f134767d8cd6aa7eada> <http://schema.org/description> "One of the greatest problems facing conservation in the British Isles is the spread and establishment of introduced species. Common cord-grass (Spartina anglica) is a highly invasive species which causes extensive ecological damage to intertidal habitats particularly mudflats and saltmarsh. The current survey represents the second of a three phase survey to establish the extent of cord-grass invasion and colonization throughout Northern Ireland." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:2aa7e9398426084ba7e40f134767d8cd6aa7eada> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:be1645a288fecd982443cfb8fc762c1c .
