_:f29c40da37a359358d3908e30c8bc5e6 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:29648ee7c60a38b638efa446064a882d902d3aed> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:f29c40da37a359358d3908e30c8bc5e6 .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:29648ee7c60a38b638efa446064a882d902d3aed> <http://schema.org/description> "Centre for Marine and Coastal Studies Ltd (CMACS) has been contracted by Greater Gabbard Offshore Wind Ltd to undertake marine ecology components of the environmental impact assessment for the proposed Greater Gabbard offshore wind farm.\r\n\r\nFollowing discussions with Zoe Crutchfield of JNCC it was agreed that the timing of benthic ecology survey works would be adjusted to reduce the possibility of accidental damage to reef habitat through grab sampling and beam trawling. Thus the drop down camera survey was undertaken as the first stage of benthic ecological survey.\r\n\r\nPoor water clarity on site during October 2004 meant that we were unsuccessful in obtaining footage of the seabed at our target sites. It was subsequently agreed with JNCC that benthic grab survey be undertaken first, followed by beam trawls (with greater potential to damage reef habitat) only at those sites where no evidence of reef habitat was found." .
_:bee9c80aced19f6994ea4aa57a955497 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:295ab61cf59aa45178b46ec648b8597f7817d461> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:aca70171a19f0b539431596a328d9a45 .
_:aca70171a19f0b539431596a328d9a45 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:295ab61cf59aa45178b46ec648b8597f7817d461> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:aca70171a19f0b539431596a328d9a45 <http://schema.org/value> "Outer Dowsing \r\n Offshore Wind (ODOW) project" .
_:a713c96fae89b3651ac56d025759b88f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:295ab61cf59aa45178b46ec648b8597f7817d461> <http://schema.org/description> "As part of the Navigational Risk Assessment (NRA) process for the proposed Outer Dowsing \r\n Offshore Wind (ODOW) project (here after referred to as â??the Projectâ??), vessel traffic survey \r\n data is being gathered within a study area around the development. To ensure full compliance \r\n with Marine Guidance Note (MGN) 654 (Maritime and Coastguard Agency (MCA), 2021), this \r\n 14-day survey meets the winter season requirements of the MCA and combined with the 14-\r\n day summer survey carried out in August 2022, a full 28-days of seasonal vessel traffic has \r\n been obtained.\r\n This report presents the analysis of the 14-day vessel traffic dataset collected from the survey \r\n vessel Karima between 15th and 29th November 2022. \r\n The primary objective of the survey was to identify and validate the routeing of vessels and \r\n the level of vessel activity within a 10 nautical mile (nm) buffer zone (the â??study areaâ??) around \r\n the project site (the â??array areaâ??). This was achieved by recording, in real time, the positions \r\n of vessels within range of the Automatic Identification System (AIS) receiver and Automatic \r\n Radio Detection and Ranging (Radar) Plotting Aid (ARPA), supplemented by observation of \r\n vessels within visual range to obtain information on type and size where the information was \r\n not available via AIS." .
_:a713c96fae89b3651ac56d025759b88f <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:295ab61cf59aa45178b46ec648b8597f7817d461> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a713c96fae89b3651ac56d025759b88f .
_:aca70171a19f0b539431596a328d9a45 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
_:a713c96fae89b3651ac56d025759b88f <http://schema.org/value> "Maritime and Coastguard Agency" .
_:e562e1ca7cec619ccab67082df9098f9 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e9ec3190088200cdad1b348e582d8bc3 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:fa4fb75f8a1f1683effe90274647aba2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e562e1ca7cec619ccab67082df9098f9 <http://schema.org/name> "marine species" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:294fd24eb24796ec37babeec34948e0f875197dd> <http://schema.org/description> "Post construction fish surveys are required to investigate changes in the fish and commercial shellfish populations in and around the wind farm site. The findings will be used for comparison with pre-construction surveys carried out in 2010 in order to assess the potential of the wind farm to act in enhancing or aggregating fish and shellfish. Any natural or manmade structure in the marine environment that stands in relief from the substratum will generally act as a fish aggregation device (FAD). This phenomenon is regularly exploited by sea anglers and commercial fishermen alike when fishing from piers and around wrecks and reefs. The document in this series provides the results of the autumn fish survey carried out in November and December 2014. Methodologies and catch data results have been provided, however no in-depth analysis of the data has been undertaken as this will be carried out after the first year of post construction (i.e. operational year one) fish surveys are completed." .
_:fa4fb75f8a1f1683effe90274647aba2 <http://schema.org/value> "Methodologies" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:294fd24eb24796ec37babeec34948e0f875197dd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
