<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1d3d1724a810d917b314071672b8ccfece82e236> <http://schema.org/description> "Benthic monitoring of the sea bed adjacent to the fish farm as a requirement of the CAR licence for the site. Grab samples collected in proximity to the farm and at two reference locations. Samples analysed for: benthos, redox, psa, carbon and sea lice medicine residues." .
_:caa417572c7e9ea9caab09abe1dac820 <http://schema.org/value> "Marine Environmental Data and Information Network" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1d3690309b0a9139636380609d5400dcf5e258a5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:caa417572c7e9ea9caab09abe1dac820 <http://schema.org/value> "British Geological Survey" .
_:caa417572c7e9ea9caab09abe1dac820 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1d3690309b0a9139636380609d5400dcf5e258a5> <http://schema.org/description> "Underwater video and camera stills and grabs acquired via Hamon Grab gathered onboard Cefas Endeavour in January 2014. These data are archived with the Marine Environmental Data and Information Network (MEDIN) Data Archive Centres (DACs) including the British Geological Survey (BGS) DAC for geology and geophysics, The Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data (DASSH) and the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) bathymetry DAC. The full site data package including raw is also available on request from BGS." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1d3690309b0a9139636380609d5400dcf5e258a5> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:caa417572c7e9ea9caab09abe1dac820 .
_:caa417572c7e9ea9caab09abe1dac820 <http://schema.org/value> "Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data" .
_:caa417572c7e9ea9caab09abe1dac820 <http://schema.org/value> "United Kingdom Hydrographic Office" .
_:caa417572c7e9ea9caab09abe1dac820 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1d1a3da5414abfbb9dfda9adddf345121520dcec> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class summarises the additional information used to describe the interviewees that reported anchoring boats for diving. Numbers of interviewees/grid cell are recorded and the mean, minimum and maximum active days per annum and years experience are also presented per grid cell. Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
_:e2bab686ad19193d0bf42bb9a5c4db35 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:e2bab686ad19193d0bf42bb9a5c4db35 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
