_:abfd3b4f33e8320445e85b87f1a5d4cc <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:c8402ac0c3867587e7687c616a35ea74 <http://schema.org/value> "13C isotope" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1d07fa72e444703fc1eec16054cb2bfeef75f770> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1d07fa72e444703fc1eec16054cb2bfeef75f770> <http://schema.org/description> "DONG Energy Renewables requested the PLA to provide geophysical and hydrographic survey works\r\nalong 9km of the Phase 3 Gunfleet Sands Demo Offshore Windfarm Site (OWF) proposed cable\r\nexport route and proposed turbine sites for UXO clearance purposes.\r\n\r\nThe PLA conducted the hydrographic (Multi Beam Echo Sounder (MBES)) element of the survey over\r\nthe Gunfleet Sands site (Survey area delineated by the shape file\r\nGeophysical_Survey_Area_Planned_201203012.shp provided by DONG energy) on the 26th and 27th\r\nof March 2012. The equipment spread included a Reson 8125H MBES with Post-processed\r\nKinematic (PPK) positioning via Applanix POS-MV GPS-aided inertial navigation system.\r\n\r\nIn April 2012 EGS (International) Ltd was commissioned to provide support to the project\r\nundertaking the geophysical element of the survey with the objective to identify any Unexploded\r\nOrdnance (UXO) threat or other seabed obstruction that may pose a hazard to the export cables,\r\narray cables and WTG foundation." .
_:cc09a5dee2fdd58a22b2f110b91ead6f <http://schema.org/value> "PLA" .
_:cc09a5dee2fdd58a22b2f110b91ead6f <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:cc09a5dee2fdd58a22b2f110b91ead6f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
