_:b4f62502ae4d5f7cc6fc676cfec0dc87 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1c7f92f2e14aa6c0d1879d13c87e27996582b120> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:b4f62502ae4d5f7cc6fc676cfec0dc87 <http://schema.org/name> "projects" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1c7f92f2e14aa6c0d1879d13c87e27996582b120> <http://schema.org/description> "This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class records the number of vessels carrying anglers on a month by month basis. These vessel counts are summarised on a standardised grid of 3/4 of a nautical mile longitude and 3/8 of a nautical mile latitude. \r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record." .
_:b4f62502ae4d5f7cc6fc676cfec0dc87 <http://schema.org/value> "Stakmap/Fishermap" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1c7f92f2e14aa6c0d1879d13c87e27996582b120> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b4f62502ae4d5f7cc6fc676cfec0dc87 .
_:c72b6884d8ba2957f803b44ed760815f <http://schema.org/value> "Humber Estuary" .
_:ad01b061f9befaa05ae5e4b1533c8899 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:ad01b061f9befaa05ae5e4b1533c8899 <http://schema.org/value> "Natural England" .
_:ad01b061f9befaa05ae5e4b1533c8899 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1c7e880ec9900cd1878967df9caa592014e2b55b> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:ad01b061f9befaa05ae5e4b1533c8899 .
_:c72b6884d8ba2957f803b44ed760815f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1c7e880ec9900cd1878967df9caa592014e2b55b> <http://schema.org/description> "Review of status of subtidal sandbanks alongside an impact assessment on this feature by the proposed IOTA capital dregde. \r\n In order to assist Natural England with their statutory responsibility of reporting to Defra on the \r\n state of subtidal sandbank features, within the Humber Estuary, ABPmer were requested to \r\n carry out a review of previous studies to help determine the presence and natural variability of \r\n such features. Further to this, some supporting evidence was requested in order to allow \r\n Natural England to reach a decision on a proposed channel deepening for the Immingham Oil \r\n Terminal, with emphasis on the potential impact such a dredge might have on the \r\n aforementioned subtidal sandbank features." .
_:c72b6884d8ba2957f803b44ed760815f <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
_:ad01b061f9befaa05ae5e4b1533c8899 <http://schema.org/value> "ABPmer" .
