_:e9c15473ff7c84b476148e50e617a8b4 <http://schema.org/value> "Centre for Marine and Coastal Studies Ltd" .
_:e9c15473ff7c84b476148e50e617a8b4 <http://schema.org/value> "SeaScape Energy Ltd" .
_:e9c15473ff7c84b476148e50e617a8b4 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1a9c3ee17a40f6e08c535b8ae671f5d11a0e4be0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:e9c15473ff7c84b476148e50e617a8b4 <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1a9c3ee17a40f6e08c535b8ae671f5d11a0e4be0> <http://schema.org/description> "This project relates to the monitoring undertaken by Centre for Marine and Coastal Studies Ltd (CMACS) on behalf of SeaScape Energy Ltd towards meeting the requirements of the Food and Environment Protection Act (FEPA) 1985 (as amended) Licence No31864/06/0 in respect of Suspended sediment concentration (SSC) monitoring during cable installation works. The specific aim of the monitoring was to validate and confirm predictions made in the project Environmental Statement. The monitoring was also undertaken to confirm that suspended sediments remained within parameters that were agreed with regulators before construction. Suspended sediment monitoring was undertaken from a small vessel using a hand deployed suspended sediment probe calibrated against local sediments. The monitoring demonstrated clearly that both cable installation techniques had only small scale impacts on localised suspended sediment concentrations. Effects were measurable to a few hundred metres only and suspended sediments were not elevated more than five times background." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1a9c3ee17a40f6e08c535b8ae671f5d11a0e4be0> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e9c15473ff7c84b476148e50e617a8b4 .
_:b6e7430f62ef67c17a0aa3a14c247818 <http://schema.org/value> "DONG\r\nEnergy" .
_:bcd52c6eacbe7544b95207d4c354e62d <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1a9b48562075a258f89355394decab98095723b8> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:b6e7430f62ef67c17a0aa3a14c247818 .
_:a1fe193853ff3402f31946efda06aa91 <http://schema.org/name> "measurements and facts" .
_:bcd52c6eacbe7544b95207d4c354e62d <http://schema.org/value> "Thames Estuary" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1a9b48562075a258f89355394decab98095723b8> <http://schema.org/description> "The Port of London Authority (PLA) Hydrographic Service was commissioned by DONG\r\nEnergy to undertake a Multibeam Echosounder (MBES) survey at the Gunfleet Sands 3\r\nOffshore Windfarm in the Thames Estuary.\r\nThe scope and technical specifications for the survey work, was outlined in Documents nos\r\n2575696 (Appendix 6) and 2575636 (Appendix 7) respectively and included:\r\n1. MBES survey of 50m wide corridor along Export Cable Route between the\r\nWTG F00 and the HDD exit point [See Figure 1].\r\n2. MBES survey of the WTG foundations F00 and G00 (100m x 100m) and 50m\r\nwide corridor along the inter-array cable.\r\nThe report in this series covers survey elements which were undertaken on 12th, 13th and 14th December\r\n2016.\r\nThe bathymetric data along the export cable has been compared to the previous PLA data\r\nfrom May 2016 and the pre-works survey of 2012." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:1a9b48562075a258f89355394decab98095723b8> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:a1fe193853ff3402f31946efda06aa91 .
