<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:16eb88818e89fa786e7f45ac0399e74b6ced50c8> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:e8145cefdb8c788e4567bbdc513b31df .
_:e8145cefdb8c788e4567bbdc513b31df <http://schema.org/value> "West Mouse" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:16eb88818e89fa786e7f45ac0399e74b6ced50c8> <http://schema.org/description> "ETA were commissioned to survey possible landing sites for 3 export cables for MCT's proposed installation of tidal current turbines off the coast of Anglesey, North Wales, between West Mouse and The Skerries. The survey encompassed the coastal area between Cemlyn Bay and Carmel Head. Two sites were under recommendation in this area, namely Hen Borth and Carmel Head. The survey was conducted on Tuesday 11th November and Wednesday 12th November" .
_:e0fda16763a6f1d9db5cc93d6934f8dc <http://schema.org/value> "MCT" .
_:e8145cefdb8c788e4567bbdc513b31df <http://schema.org/value> "Cemlyn Bay" .
_:cb5d04cb362ed527fb69027f88132106 <http://schema.org/value> "Humber Plume" .
_:cb5d04cb362ed527fb69027f88132106 <http://schema.org/value> "UK east coast" .
_:cb5d04cb362ed527fb69027f88132106 <http://schema.org/value> "Humber Estuary" .
_:cb5d04cb362ed527fb69027f88132106 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:16d78520c8135ac5fe5788087210fa905d22673f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:cb5d04cb362ed527fb69027f88132106 <http://schema.org/name> "geospatial region" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:16d78520c8135ac5fe5788087210fa905d22673f> <http://schema.org/description> "This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during January 1993. It incorporates a CTD survey of the waters within 20 miles of the UK east coast from the Tees to the Thames including stations in the Humber Estuary, Humber Plume and the Wash. The data were collected by the Ministry of Agriculture, Fisheries and Food Lowestoft Fisheries Laboratory as part of the Joint Nutrient Study I (JoNuS)." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:16d78520c8135ac5fe5788087210fa905d22673f> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:cb5d04cb362ed527fb69027f88132106 .
_:b7f442128152a356ce0b1b13a8db14de <http://schema.org/value> "marine wildlife" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:16d5765976c2ad9b61317eba9d788f9cce7f5112> <http://schema.org/description> "The Marine and Coastal Access Act (2009) created a new type of Marine Protected Area (MPA), called a Marine Conservation Zone (MCZ).\r\n \r\n MCZs will protect nationally important marine wildlife, habitats, geology and geomorphology. The Marine Conservation Zone Project concerns the selection of MCZs in English inshore waters and offshore waters next to England, Wales and Northern Ireland. Sites will be selected to protect not just the rare and threatened, but the range of marine wildlife." .
_:b7f442128152a356ce0b1b13a8db14de <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/PropertyValue> .
_:a33d0c321f15e378a4d0520e663562ca <http://schema.org/value> "England" .
