<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:15d8c50bef59e621e7122f8e18bf0cfd60f86764> <http://schema.org/description> "Pectenogammarus planicrurus presence record from Sussex. \r\n \r\n This species of amphipod was described by Reid (1940) as a new species of Gammarus. Pectenogammarus was erected as a sub-genus, subsequently to be raised to the rank of genus (Reid 1944). Reid found the species to be plentiful 'under stones near high-water mark on the chalky shores of the south coast of England'. The type locality at Saltdean is a gently sloping shore of solid chalk. P. planicrurus was found amongst flint shingle, which was restricted to a level near high-water mark." .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:15d8c50bef59e621e7122f8e18bf0cfd60f86764> <http://schema.org/additionalProperty> _:fbfcdb60a00a77ea0ce61ff0426683ae .
