<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:06a362a2bae098b93c7581cd201fbd586cadcae9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://schema.org/Dataset> .
_:dc1787e16e7cdeeb8a45e568f6b3e91c <http://schema.org/name> "organizations" .
_:edf42ac753db821076ce27e00c997cfb <http://schema.org/value> "North Wales" .
<urn:gleaner.io:oih:medin:data:06a362a2bae098b93c7581cd201fbd586cadcae9> <http://schema.org/description> "On the instructions of Vestas Wind Systems - Celtic Wind Technology Limited, Exploration associates carried out a survey of a 4000 by 1500m wide area over North Hoyle Bank, off the North Wales coast, for the purposes of designing and installing an offshore wind farm. Line spacing was set at 250m running parallel and perpendicular to the outline orientation of the windfarm. The objective of the survey was to evaluate global seabed movements during the winter months by providing a direct comparison of seabed levels with a previous survey conducted in July 2002 by Exploration Associates. This was achieved by carrying out a bathymetric survey utilising a dual frequency echo sounder.\r\nSurvey work was conducted between 31st January 2003 and 12th February 2003 with seven full days being lost due to adverse weather conditions." .
_:edf42ac753db821076ce27e00c997cfb <http://schema.org/value> "North Hoyle Bank" .
